-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 11 (False evidence and offences against
-- public justice, ss 191-229) and Chapter 12 (Offences relating to Government
-- stamps, ss 230-263).
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt). Section text is quoted above each rule,
-- copied mechanically from the source with page footers removed and curly
-- quotes and dashes made ASCII.
--
-- The group is "justice-order" (notes/PLAN.md s 1); Chapters 13-15 are in
-- pc-justice-order-public.l4, and the tests for both in
-- pc-justice-order-tests.l4.
--
-- What the reader must know before reading:
--
-- * The charge-generator contract (BRIEF.md, PLAN.md s 3, s 8). Each offence
--   family has ONE facts record `<Family> Facts`, taken as `GIVEN f`. Each
--   defining section is a BOOLEAN over f named in the section's own verb; each
--   punishing section has `offence under s N` (BOOLEAN) and `charge under s N`
--   (a Charge). Every leaf is a flat BOOLEAN; STRING fields are recited only.
-- * Where a section's punishment turns on how the PREDICATE offence is punished
--   (ss 201, 212, 213, 214, 216, 221, 222, 225 - "if the offence is punishable
--   with death ..."), the tier is a BOOLEAN leaf in the Code's words, and the
--   charge builder picks the punishment by it, as the reference row does for
--   s 420(2). The tier is an element of the offence ladder, because the section
--   prescribes no punishment outside its tiers (FORK JO-3).
-- * Where a section punishes "in the same manner as if he gave false evidence"
--   (ss 196-200), the charge recites that phrase and names the s 193 limb that
--   the facts select (FORK JO-2).
-- * Cross-references to other groups' sections are BOOLEAN leaves whose @desc
--   names the owning module (PLAN.md s 1, "cross-module joins owed").
-- * No offence ladder repeats a General Exception (PLAN.md s 5). Exceptions
--   printed inside a section of these Chapters are part of that section.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`

§ `Chapter 11 - False evidence and offences against public justice`

§§ `Helpers for the recital`

-- ", to wit, <what was done>" - the particulars a Singapore charge gives
-- after the statutory words. Omitted when the officer gives none.

-- s 201(c), 212(1)(c), 213(c), 214(c), 216(1)(c): "one-fourth part of the
-- longest term of imprisonment provided for that offence".
@export The term which is "one-fourth part of the longest term of imprisonment provided for" an offence (ss 201(c), 212(1)(c), 213(c), 214(c), 216(1)(c) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER @desc The longest term of imprisonment provided for the offence, in months
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one-fourth part of the longest term of imprisonment` months MEANS months / 4

§§ `s 191 - Giving false evidence`

-- 191. Whoever, being legally bound by an oath, or by any express provision of law to
-- state the truth, or being bound by law to make a declaration upon any subject, makes
-- any statement which is false, and which he either knows or believes to be false, or
-- does not believe to be true, is said to give false evidence.
-- Explanation 1.-A statement is within the meaning of this section whether it is made
-- verbally or otherwise.
-- Explanation 2.-A false statement as to the belief of the person attesting is within
-- the meaning of this section, and a person may be guilty of giving false evidence by
-- stating that he believes a thing which he does not believe, as well as by stating
-- that he knows a thing which he does not know.
-- Illustrations
--    (a) A, in support of a just claim which B has against Z for $1,000, falsely
--      swears on a trial that he heard Z admit the justice of B's claim. A has given
--      false evidence.
--    (b) A, being bound by an oath to state the truth, states that he believes a
--      certain signature to be the handwriting of Z, when he does not believe it to be
--      the handwriting of Z. Here A states that which he knows to be false, and
--      therefore gives false evidence.
--    (c) A, knowing the general character of Z's handwriting, states that he believes
--      a certain signature to be the handwriting of Z, A in good faith believing it to
--      be so. Here A's statement is merely as to his belief, and is true as to his
--      belief, and therefore, although the signature may not be the handwriting of Z, A
--      has not given false evidence.
--    (d) A, being bound by an oath to state the truth, states that he knows that Z was
--      at a particular place on a particular day, not knowing anything upon the subject.
--      A gives false evidence as to whether Z was at that place on the day named, or
--      not.
--    (e) A, an interpreter or a translator, gives or certifies as a true
--      interpretation or translation of a statement or document which he is bound by
--      oath to interpret or translate truly, that which is not and which he does not
--      believe to be a true interpretation or translation. A has given false evidence.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 191-195 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `False Evidence Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `legally bound by an oath to state the truth`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused legally bound by an oath to state the truth? (s 191)
    `bound by an express provision of law to state the truth`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused bound by an express provision of law to state the truth? (s 191)
    `bound by law to make a declaration upon any subject`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused bound by law to make a declaration upon the subject? (s 191)
    `makes a statement`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make a statement? It counts whether made verbally or otherwise (Explanation 1), and a statement of the accused's own belief counts (Explanation 2).
    `the statement is false`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement false? A statement that the accused believes or knows a thing which he does not believe or know is false (Explanation 2; illustrations (b), (d)).
    `he knows or believes the statement to be false`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know or believe the statement to be false? (s 191) - a fault element
    `he does not believe the statement to be true`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused not believe the statement to be true? (s 191) - a fault element
    `the statement`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused stated, as it is to read after "to wit, by stating" - for example "that he heard Z admit the justice of B's claim"
    `causes any circumstance to exist`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause a circumstance to exist? (s 192) - for example, putting jewels in another's box
    `makes any false entry in any book or record or electronic record`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make a false entry in a book, record or electronic record? (s 192)
    `makes any document or electronic record containing a false statement`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make a document or electronic record containing a false statement? (s 192)
    `intending that it may appear in evidence in a judicial proceeding`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend that the circumstance, entry or statement may appear in evidence in a judicial proceeding? (s 192)
    `intending that it may appear in evidence in a proceeding taken by law before a public servant as such`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... in a proceeding taken by law before a public servant as such (s 21)? (s 192)
    `intending that it may appear in evidence before an arbitrator`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... before an arbitrator? (s 192)
    `intending that it may cause a person forming an opinion upon the evidence to entertain an erroneous opinion touching a point material to the result`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend that, so appearing in evidence, it may cause a person who is to form an opinion upon the evidence in that proceeding to entertain an erroneous opinion touching a point material to its result? (s 192)
    `the fabrication`                        IS A STRING @desc What the accused did to fabricate the evidence, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by putting jewels into a box belonging to Z"
    `gives it intentionally`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused give the false evidence intentionally (s 26C)? (s 193) - a fault element
    `in any stage of a judicial proceeding`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the false evidence given in a stage of a judicial proceeding (s 193)? A court-martial trial is one (Explanation 1); so is an investigation directed by law preliminary to a proceeding before a court (Explanation 2), and an investigation directed by a court and conducted under its authority (Explanation 3).
    `for the purpose of being used in any stage of a judicial proceeding`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the false evidence fabricated for the purpose of being used in a stage of a judicial proceeding? (s 193; Explanations 1-3 as above)
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence which is capital`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend thereby to cause, or know it to be likely that he would thereby cause, any person to be convicted of an offence which is capital by this Code or any other law in force? (s 194)
    `an innocent person is convicted and executed in consequence of the false evidence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an innocent person convicted and executed in consequence of the false evidence? (s 194)
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence not capital but punishable with imprisonment for a term of 7 years or upwards`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend, or know it likely, that he would thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence which is not capital but is punishable with imprisonment for a term of 7 years or upwards (s 41 reads 'or upwards')? (s 195(1))
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence not capital but punishable with imprisonment for life`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend, or know it likely, that he would thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence which is not capital but is punishable with imprisonment for life? (s 195(2))
    `the offence intended`                   IS A STRING @desc The offence of which the accused meant someone to be convicted, as it is to read in the charge - for example "gang-robbery"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 191, Explanations 1 and 2
@export Whether the accused "gives false evidence" within section 191 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `gives false evidence` f IF
        "Whoever, being"
    AND (    f's `legally bound by an oath to state the truth`
         OR  f's `bound by an express provision of law to state the truth`
         OR  f's `bound by law to make a declaration upon any subject` )
    AND f's `makes a statement`
    AND f's `the statement is false`
    AND "and which he either"
    AND (    f's `he knows or believes the statement to be false`
         OR  f's `he does not believe the statement to be true` )
    AND "is said to give false evidence"

§§ `s 192 - Fabricating false evidence`

-- 192. Whoever causes any circumstance to exist, or makes any false entry in any book
-- or record or electronic record, or makes any document or electronic record
-- containing a false statement, intending that such circumstance, false entry, or
-- false statement may appear in evidence in a judicial proceeding, or in a proceeding
-- taken by law before a public servant as such, or before an arbitrator, and that such
-- circumstance, false entry, or false statement, so appearing in evidence, may cause
-- any person, who in such proceeding is to form an opinion upon the evidence, to
-- entertain an erroneous opinion touching any point material to the result of such
-- proceeding, is said "to fabricate false evidence".
-- Illustrations
--    (a) A puts jewels into a box belonging to Z with the intention that they may be
--      found in that box and that this circumstance may cause Z to be convicted of
--      theft. A has fabricated false evidence.
--    (b) A makes a false entry in his shop-book for the purpose of using it as
--      corroborative evidence in a court of justice. A has fabricated false evidence.
--    (c) A, with the intention of causing Z to be convicted of a criminal conspiracy,
--      writes a letter in imitation of Z's handwriting, purporting to be addressed to an
--      accomplice in such criminal conspiracy, and puts the letter in a place which he
--      knows that the officers of the police are likely to search. A has fabricated
--      false evidence.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 192
@export Whether the accused "fabricates false evidence" within section 192 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fabricates false evidence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `causes any circumstance to exist`
         OR  f's `makes any false entry in any book or record or electronic record`
         OR  f's `makes any document or electronic record containing a false statement` )
    AND (    f's `intending that it may appear in evidence in a judicial proceeding`
         OR  f's `intending that it may appear in evidence in a proceeding taken by law before a public servant as such`
         OR  f's `intending that it may appear in evidence before an arbitrator` )
    AND f's `intending that it may cause a person forming an opinion upon the evidence to entertain an erroneous opinion touching a point material to the result`
    AND "is said to fabricate false evidence"

§§ `s 193 - Punishment for false evidence`

-- 193. Whoever intentionally gives false evidence in any stage of a judicial
-- proceeding, or fabricates false evidence for the purpose of being used in any stage
-- of a judicial proceeding, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine; and whoever intentionally gives
-- or fabricates false evidence in any other case, shall be punished with imprisonment
-- for a term which may extend to 3 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
-- Explanation 1.-A trial before a court martial is a judicial proceeding.
-- Explanation 2.-An investigation directed by law preliminary to a proceeding before a
-- court of justice, is a stage of a judicial proceeding, though that investigation may
-- not take place before a court of justice.
-- Illustration A, in an inquiry before a Magistrate for the purpose of ascertaining
-- whether Z ought to be committed for trial, makes on oath a statement which he knows
-- to be false. As this inquiry is a stage of a judicial proceeding, A has given false
-- evidence.
-- Explanation 3.-An investigation directed by a court of justice according to law, and
-- conducted under the authority of a court of justice, is a stage of a judicial
-- proceeding, though that investigation may not take place before a court of justice.
-- Illustration A, in an inquiry before an officer deputed by a court of justice to
-- ascertain on the spot the boundaries of land, makes on oath a statement which he
-- knows to be false. As this inquiry is a stage of a judicial proceeding, A has given
-- false evidence.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 193
`punishment prescribed by s 193 (judicial proceeding)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "193"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 193
`punishment prescribed by s 193 (any other case)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "193"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the false evidence falls under the first, heavier limb of section 193 of the Penal Code 1871 (a stage of a judicial proceeding) rather than "any other case"
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false evidence is in a stage of a judicial proceeding` f IF
        (    `gives false evidence` f
         AND f's `in any stage of a judicial proceeding` )
    OR  (    `fabricates false evidence` f
         AND f's `for the purpose of being used in any stage of a judicial proceeding` )

-- Both limbs of s 193 have the same elements; they differ in punishment only, by
-- whether the evidence is in (or for) a stage of a judicial proceeding. One offence,
-- two punishment records (PLAN s 6).
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 193 of the Penal Code 1871 (punishment for false evidence)
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 193` f IF
        (    "Whoever"
         AND f's `gives it intentionally`
         AND `gives false evidence` f )
    OR  (    "or"
         AND `fabricates false evidence` f )

GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the false evidence recital` f MEANS
    `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `gives it intentionally` AND `gives false evidence` f)
            (CONCAT "did intentionally give false evidence",
                    (IF f's `in any stage of a judicial proceeding` THEN " in a stage of a judicial proceeding" ELSE ""),
                    (`to wit` (IF f's `the statement` EQUALS "" THEN "" ELSE CONCAT "by stating ", f's `the statement`)),
                    ", which statement you knew or believed to be false or did not believe to be true")),
        (`included if` (`fabricates false evidence` f)
            (CONCAT "did fabricate false evidence",
                    (IF f's `for the purpose of being used in any stage of a judicial proceeding` THEN " for the purpose of being used in a stage of a judicial proceeding" ELSE ""),
                    (`to wit` (f's `the fabrication`))))))

GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of false evidence not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (`gives false evidence` f OR `fabricates false evidence` f) "gives false evidence (section 191) or fabricates false evidence (section 192)"),
        (`missing unless` (`fabricates false evidence` f OR f's `gives it intentionally`) "intentionally (section 193)"))

@export Frame a charge under section 193 of the Penal Code 1871 (punishment for false evidence), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 193` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "193" "giving or fabricating false evidence"
        (IF `the false evidence is in a stage of a judicial proceeding` f THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (judicial proceeding)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (any other case)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 193` f)
        (`the false evidence recital` f)
        (concat (LIST
                (`elements of false evidence not made out` f)))

§§ `s 194 - Giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of a capital offence`

-- 194. Whoever gives or fabricates false evidence, intending thereby to cause, or
-- knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, any person to be convicted of an
-- offence which is capital by this Code, or under any other law for the time being in
-- force, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term
-- which may extend to 20 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for
-- life, also be liable to fine; and if an innocent person is convicted and executed in
-- consequence of such false evidence, the person who gives such false evidence shall
-- be punished either with death or the punishment hereinbefore described.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 194
`punishment prescribed by s 194` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "194"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 194
`punishment prescribed by s 194 (innocent person executed)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "194"
    words                    IS "either with death or the punishment hereinbefore described"
    death                    IS `or with`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 194 of the Penal Code 1871 (giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of a capital offence)
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 194` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    `gives false evidence` f
         OR  `fabricates false evidence` f )
    AND f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence which is capital`

@export Frame a charge under section 194 of the Penal Code 1871 ("giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of a capital offence"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 194` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "194" "giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of a capital offence"
        (IF f's `an innocent person is convicted and executed in consequence of the false evidence` AND `gives false evidence` f THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 194 (innocent person executed)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 194`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 194` f)
        (CONCAT "did give or fabricate false evidence, intending thereby to cause, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby cause, a person to be convicted of an offence which is capital, namely ", f's `the offence intended`, (`to wit` (`joined with` ", and " (append (`included if` (NOT (f's `the statement` EQUALS "")) (f's `the statement`)) (`included if` (NOT (f's `the fabrication` EQUALS "")) (f's `the fabrication`))))))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (`gives false evidence` f OR `fabricates false evidence` f) "gives false evidence (section 191) or fabricates false evidence (section 192)"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence which is capital`) "intending thereby to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, any person to be convicted of an offence which is capital")))

§§ `s 195 - Giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of an offence punishable with imprisonment`

-- 195.-(1) Whoever gives or fabricates false evidence, intending thereby to cause, or
-- knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, any person to be convicted of an
-- offence which by this Code or under any other law for the time being in force is not
-- capital, but punishable with imprisonment for a term of 7 years or upwards, shall be
-- punished as a person convicted of that offence would be liable to be punished,
-- except that he shall not be punished with caning.
-- [15/2019]
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]
-- (2) Whoever gives or fabricates false evidence, intending thereby to cause, or
-- knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, any person to be convicted of an
-- offence which by this Code or under any other law for the time being in force is not
-- capital, but punishable with imprisonment for life, shall be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years.
-- Illustration A gives false evidence before a court of justice, intending thereby to
-- cause Z to be convicted of a gang-robbery. The punishment of gang-robbery is
-- imprisonment for a term of not less than 5 years and not more than 20 years and also
-- caning with not less than 12 strokes. A, therefore, is liable to such imprisonment,
-- but is not liable to caning.
-- [15/2019]
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]

-- s 195(1) punishes "as a person convicted of that offence would be liable to
-- be punished, except that he shall not be punished with caning". So the
-- punishment is a function of the OTHER offence's punishment: the same
-- record, with caning struck out and the section renamed.
@export The punishment under section 195(1) of the Penal Code 1871: that of the offence the false evidence was meant to procure a conviction for, "except that he shall not be punished with caning"
GIVEN p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment prescribed for the offence the accused intended someone to be convicted of
GIVETH A Punishment
`punishment prescribed by s 195(1) for` p MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        section                  IS "195(1)"
        words                    IS "as a person convicted of that offence would be liable to be punished, except that he shall not be punished with caning"
        death                    IS p's death
        `imprisonment for life`  IS p's `imprisonment for life`
        imprisonment             IS p's imprisonment
        `maximum term in months` IS p's `maximum term in months`
        `minimum term in months` IS p's `minimum term in months`
        `forfeiture of property` IS p's `forfeiture of property`
        fine                     IS p's fine
        `maximum fine`           IS p's `maximum fine`
        `minimum fine`           IS p's `minimum fine`
        caning                   IS `not prescribed`
        `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
        `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
        `or with both`           IS p's `or with both`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 195(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 195(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "195(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 195(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of an offence punishable with imprisonment for 7 years or upwards)
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 195(1)` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    `gives false evidence` f
         OR  `fabricates false evidence` f )
    AND f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence not capital but punishable with imprisonment for a term of 7 years or upwards`

@export Frame a charge under section 195(1) of the Penal Code 1871 ("giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of an offence punishable with imprisonment"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 195(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "195(1)" "giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of an offence punishable with imprisonment"
        ("as a person convicted of that offence would be liable to be punished, except that he shall not be punished with caning")
        (`offence under s 195(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "did give or fabricate false evidence, intending thereby to cause, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby cause, a person to be convicted of an offence which is not capital but punishable with imprisonment for a term of 7 years or upwards, namely ", f's `the offence intended`, (`to wit` (`joined with` ", and " (append (`included if` (NOT (f's `the statement` EQUALS "")) (f's `the statement`)) (`included if` (NOT (f's `the fabrication` EQUALS "")) (f's `the fabrication`))))))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (`gives false evidence` f OR `fabricates false evidence` f) "gives false evidence (section 191) or fabricates false evidence (section 192)"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence not capital but punishable with imprisonment for a term of 7 years or upwards`) "intending or knowing it likely to cause a conviction of an offence not capital but punishable with imprisonment for 7 years or upwards")))

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 195(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of an offence punishable with imprisonment for life)
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 195(2)` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    `gives false evidence` f
         OR  `fabricates false evidence` f )
    AND f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence not capital but punishable with imprisonment for life`

@export Frame a charge under section 195(2) of the Penal Code 1871 ("giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of an offence punishable with imprisonment for life"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Evidence Facts` @desc What the accused stated or fabricated, and for what proceeding, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 195(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "195(2)" "giving or fabricating false evidence with intent to procure conviction of an offence punishable with imprisonment for life"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 195(2)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 195(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did give or fabricate false evidence, intending thereby to cause, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby cause, a person to be convicted of an offence which is not capital but punishable with imprisonment for life, namely ", f's `the offence intended`, (`to wit` (`joined with` ", and " (append (`included if` (NOT (f's `the statement` EQUALS "")) (f's `the statement`)) (`included if` (NOT (f's `the fabrication` EQUALS "")) (f's `the fabrication`))))))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (`gives false evidence` f OR `fabricates false evidence` f) "gives false evidence (section 191) or fabricates false evidence (section 192)"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause any person to be convicted of an offence not capital but punishable with imprisonment for life`) "intending or knowing it likely to cause a conviction of an offence not capital but punishable with imprisonment for life")))

§§ `s 196 - Using evidence known to be false`

-- 196. Whoever corruptly uses or attempts to use as true or genuine evidence any
-- evidence which he knows to be false or fabricated, shall be punished in the same
-- manner as if he gave or fabricated false evidence.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 196-200 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Using False Evidence Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `uses or attempts to use as true or genuine evidence any evidence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused use, or attempt to use, as true or genuine evidence any evidence? (s 196)
    `corruptly`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act corruptly? (ss 196, 198, 200) - the Code does not define the word
    `knows the evidence to be false or fabricated`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know the evidence to be false or fabricated? (s 196) - a fault element
    `issues or signs any certificate`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused issue or sign a certificate? (s 197)
    `the certificate is required by law to be given or signed`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate one required by law to be given or signed? (s 197)
    `the certificate relates to a fact of which it is by law admissible in evidence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate relate to a fact of which such a certificate is by law admissible in evidence? (s 197)
    `knowing or believing that the certificate is false in any material point`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know or believe the certificate to be false in a material point? (ss 197, 198) - a fault element
    `uses or attempts to use the certificate as a true certificate`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused use, or attempt to use, such a certificate as a true certificate? (s 198)
    `knowing the certificate to be false in any material point`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused KNOW the certificate to be false in a material point? (s 198 - knowledge; belief is not enough, unlike s 197) - a fault element
    `makes a statement in a declaration made or subscribed by him`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make a statement in a declaration he made or subscribed? A declaration inadmissible merely for some informality still counts (s 200 Explanation). (s 199)
    `a court of justice, public servant or other person is bound or authorised by law to receive the declaration as evidence of any fact`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a court of justice, a public servant or another person bound or authorised by law to receive the declaration as evidence of any fact? (s 199)
    `the statement in the declaration is false`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement false? (s 199)
    `knows or believes the statement in the declaration to be false or does not believe it to be true`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know or believe it to be false, or not believe it to be true? (s 199) - a fault element
    `touching any point material to the object for which the declaration is made or used`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the statement touch a point material to the object for which the declaration was made or used? (s 199)
    `uses or attempts to use as true any such declaration`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused use, or attempt to use, as true a declaration of the kind in s 199? (s 200)
    `knowing the declaration to be false in any material point`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know the declaration to be false in a material point? (s 200) - a fault element
    `in any stage of a judicial proceeding`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the evidence, certificate or declaration used or given in a stage of a judicial proceeding? This selects which of s 193's two punishments applies "as if he gave false evidence" (FORK JO-2).
    `what was used or made`                  IS A STRING @desc The evidence, certificate or declaration, as it is to read after "to wit,"

@export Whether the accused corruptly uses or attempts to use as true evidence known to be false or fabricated (s 196 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `corruptly uses evidence known to be false` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's corruptly
    AND f's `uses or attempts to use as true or genuine evidence any evidence`
    AND "which he"
    AND f's `knows the evidence to be false or fabricated`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 196 of the Penal Code 1871 (using evidence known to be false)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 196` f IF
    `corruptly uses evidence known to be false` f

@export Frame a charge under section 196 of the Penal Code 1871 ("using evidence known to be false"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 196` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "196" "using evidence known to be false"
        (CONCAT "in the same manner as if he gave or fabricated false evidence (section 193: ", (IF f's `in any stage of a judicial proceeding` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (judicial proceeding)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (any other case)`)'s words), ")")
        (`offence under s 196` f)
        (CONCAT "did corruptly use or attempt to use as true or genuine evidence evidence which you knew to be false or fabricated", (`to wit` (f's `what was used or made`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's corruptly) "corruptly"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `uses or attempts to use as true or genuine evidence any evidence`) "uses or attempts to use as true or genuine evidence any evidence"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knows the evidence to be false or fabricated`) "which he knows to be false or fabricated")))

§§ `s 197 - Issuing or signing a false certificate`

-- 197. Whoever issues or signs any certificate required by law to be given or signed,
-- or relating to any fact of which such certificate is by law admissible in evidence,
-- knowing or believing that such certificate is false in any material point, shall be
-- punished in the same manner as if he gave false evidence.

@export Whether the accused issues or signs a certificate known or believed false in a material point (s 197 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `issues or signs a false certificate` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `issues or signs any certificate`
    AND (    f's `the certificate is required by law to be given or signed`
         OR  f's `the certificate relates to a fact of which it is by law admissible in evidence` )
    AND f's `knowing or believing that the certificate is false in any material point`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 197 of the Penal Code 1871 (issuing or signing a false certificate)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 197` f IF
    `issues or signs a false certificate` f

@export Frame a charge under section 197 of the Penal Code 1871 ("issuing or signing a false certificate"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 197` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "197" "issuing or signing a false certificate"
        (CONCAT "in the same manner as if he gave false evidence (section 193: ", (IF f's `in any stage of a judicial proceeding` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (judicial proceeding)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (any other case)`)'s words), ")")
        (`offence under s 197` f)
        (CONCAT "did issue or sign a certificate required by law to be given or signed, or relating to a fact of which it is by law admissible in evidence, knowing or believing that the certificate was false in a material point", (`to wit` (f's `what was used or made`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `issues or signs any certificate`) "issues or signs any certificate"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the certificate is required by law to be given or signed` OR f's `the certificate relates to a fact of which it is by law admissible in evidence`) "required by law to be given or signed, or relating to a fact of which such certificate is by law admissible in evidence"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or believing that the certificate is false in any material point`) "knowing or believing that such certificate is false in any material point")))

§§ `s 198 - Using as a true certificate one known to be false in a material point`

-- 198. Whoever corruptly uses or attempts to use any such certificate as a true
-- certificate, knowing the same to be false in any material point, shall be punished
-- in the same manner as if he gave false evidence.

-- s 198 reads "knowing the same to be false", narrower than s 197's "knowing or
-- believing", so it has its own leaf (FORK JO-4).
@export Whether the accused corruptly uses as true a certificate known to be false in a material point (s 198 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uses as true a certificate known to be false` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's corruptly
    AND f's `uses or attempts to use the certificate as a true certificate`
    AND f's `knowing the certificate to be false in any material point`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 198 of the Penal Code 1871 (using as a true certificate one known to be false in a material point)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 198` f IF
    `uses as true a certificate known to be false` f

@export Frame a charge under section 198 of the Penal Code 1871 ("using as a true certificate one known to be false in a material point"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 198` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "198" "using as a true certificate one known to be false in a material point"
        (CONCAT "in the same manner as if he gave false evidence (section 193: ", (IF f's `in any stage of a judicial proceeding` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (judicial proceeding)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (any other case)`)'s words), ")")
        (`offence under s 198` f)
        (CONCAT "did corruptly use or attempt to use as a true certificate a certificate which you knew to be false in a material point", (`to wit` (f's `what was used or made`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's corruptly) "corruptly"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `uses or attempts to use the certificate as a true certificate`) "uses or attempts to use any such certificate as a true certificate"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing the certificate to be false in any material point`) "knowing the same to be false in any material point")))

§§ `s 199 - False statement made in any declaration which is by law receivable as evidence`

-- 199. Whoever, in any declaration made or subscribed by him, which declaration any
-- court of justice, or any public servant or other person, is bound or authorised by
-- law to receive as evidence of any fact, makes any statement which is false, and
-- which he either knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true,
-- touching any point material to the object for which the declaration is made or used,
-- shall be punished in the same manner as if he gave false evidence.

@export Whether the accused makes a false statement in a declaration which is by law receivable as evidence (s 199 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes a false statement in a declaration receivable as evidence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `makes a statement in a declaration made or subscribed by him`
    AND f's `a court of justice, public servant or other person is bound or authorised by law to receive the declaration as evidence of any fact`
    AND f's `the statement in the declaration is false`
    AND f's `knows or believes the statement in the declaration to be false or does not believe it to be true`
    AND f's `touching any point material to the object for which the declaration is made or used`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 199 of the Penal Code 1871 (false statement made in any declaration which is by law receivable as evidence)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 199` f IF
    `makes a false statement in a declaration receivable as evidence` f

@export Frame a charge under section 199 of the Penal Code 1871 ("false statement made in a declaration which is by law receivable as evidence"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 199` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "199" "false statement made in a declaration which is by law receivable as evidence"
        (CONCAT "in the same manner as if he gave false evidence (section 193: ", (IF f's `in any stage of a judicial proceeding` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (judicial proceeding)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (any other case)`)'s words), ")")
        (`offence under s 199` f)
        (CONCAT "did, in a declaration made or subscribed by you, which a court of justice, public servant or other person was bound or authorised by law to receive as evidence of a fact, make a statement which was false and which you knew or believed to be false or did not believe to be true, touching a point material to the object for which the declaration was made or used", (`to wit` (f's `what was used or made`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `makes a statement in a declaration made or subscribed by him`) "makes a statement in a declaration made or subscribed by him"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `a court of justice, public servant or other person is bound or authorised by law to receive the declaration as evidence of any fact`) "which declaration a court of justice, public servant or other person is bound or authorised by law to receive as evidence"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the statement in the declaration is false`) "which is false"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knows or believes the statement in the declaration to be false or does not believe it to be true`) "which he knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `touching any point material to the object for which the declaration is made or used`) "touching any point material to the object for which the declaration is made or used")))

§§ `s 200 - Using as true any such declaration known to be false`

-- 200. Whoever corruptly uses or attempts to use as true any such declaration knowing
-- the same to be false in any material point, shall be punished in the same manner as
-- if he gave false evidence.
-- Explanation.-A declaration which is inadmissible merely upon the ground of some
-- informality, is a declaration within the meaning of sections 199 and 200.

@export Whether the accused corruptly uses as true a declaration known to be false in a material point (s 200 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uses as true a declaration known to be false` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's corruptly
    AND f's `uses or attempts to use as true any such declaration`
    AND f's `knowing the declaration to be false in any material point`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 200 of the Penal Code 1871 (using as true any such declaration known to be false)
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 200` f IF
    `uses as true a declaration known to be false` f

@export Frame a charge under section 200 of the Penal Code 1871 ("using as true a declaration known to be false"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Using False Evidence Facts` @desc What evidence, certificate or declaration the accused made or used, and what the accused knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 200` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "200" "using as true a declaration known to be false"
        (CONCAT "in the same manner as if he gave false evidence (section 193: ", (IF f's `in any stage of a judicial proceeding` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (judicial proceeding)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 193 (any other case)`)'s words), ")")
        (`offence under s 200` f)
        (CONCAT "did corruptly use or attempt to use as true a declaration which you knew to be false in a material point", (`to wit` (f's `what was used or made`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's corruptly) "corruptly"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `uses or attempts to use as true any such declaration`) "uses or attempts to use as true any such declaration"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing the declaration to be false in any material point`) "knowing the same to be false in any material point")))

§§ `s 201 - Causing disappearance of evidence of an offence committed, or giving false information touching it, to screen the offender`

-- 201. Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been
-- committed, causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear with
-- the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment, or with that
-- intention gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to
-- be false, shall -
--    (a) if the offence which he knows or believes to have been committed is
--      punishable with death, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--      to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine;
--    (b) if the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment
--      which may extend to 20 years, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine; and
--    (c) if the offence is punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to
--      20 years, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to one-
--      fourth part of the longest term of the imprisonment provided for the offence, or
--      with fine, or with both.
-- Illustration A, knowing that B has murdered Z, assists B to hide the body with the
-- intention of screening B from punishment. A is liable to imprisonment for 10 years,
-- and also to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 201-203 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Offence Information Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know, or have reason to believe (s 26), that an offence had been committed? For ss 201-203, "offence" includes an act done outside Singapore which would be punishable here under ss 302, 304, 382, 392-397, 399, 402, 435, 436, 449, 450, 459 or 460 (s 203 Explanation).
    `causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear? (s 201)
    `gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused give information about the offence which the accused knew or believed to be false? (ss 201, 203)
    `with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment? (s 201) - a fault element
    `intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally omit to give information about the offence? (s 202)
    `which he is legally bound to give`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused legally bound to give that information (s 43)? (s 202)
    `the offence is punishable with death`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence (the one screened, harboured or concealed) punishable with death? - its punishment is in its own section, possibly in another group's module
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence punishable with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years?
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence one where "punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to 20 years"? - the words differ from section to section and are the Code's own
    `the offence`                            IS A STRING @desc The offence, as it is to be named in the charge - for example "murder"
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 201(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 201(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "201(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 201(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 201(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "201(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 201(c)
`punishment prescribed by s 201(c)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "201(c)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one-fourth part of the longest term of imprisonment provided for that offence, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused causes evidence of an offence to disappear, or gives false information touching it, to screen the offender (s 201 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `causes disappearance of evidence of an offence to screen the offender` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed`
    AND (f's `causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear` OR f's `gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false`)
    AND f's `with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment`

-- The tier is an element of the offence: s 201 prescribes a punishment only where the
-- screened offence is punishable as (a), (b) or (c) says (FORK JO-3).
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 201 of the Penal Code 1871 (causing disappearance of evidence of an offence committed, or giving false information touching it, to screen the offender)
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 201` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `causes disappearance of evidence of an offence to screen the offender` f
    AND (f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to 20 years`)

@export Frame a charge under section 201 of the Penal Code 1871 (causing disappearance of evidence of an offence committed, or giving false information touching it, to screen the offender), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 201` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "201" "causing disappearance of evidence of an offence committed, or giving false information touching it, to screen the offender"
        (IF f's `the offence is punishable with death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 201(a)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 201(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 201(c)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 201` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing or having reason to believe that an offence, namely ", f's `the offence`, ", had been committed, did cause evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear, or give information respecting it which you knew or believed to be false, with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed`) "knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear` OR f's `gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false`)) "causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear, or gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment`) "with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to 20 years`)) "the offence is punishable with death, with imprisonment for life or up to 20 years, or where it is punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to 20 years"),
                (`missing unless` (`causes disappearance of evidence of an offence to screen the offender` f) "the elements of section 201 taken together")))

§§ `s 202 - Intentional omission to give information of an offence, by person bound to inform`

-- 202. Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been
-- committed, intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence which
-- he is legally bound to give, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
-- may extend to 6 months, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 202
`punishment prescribed by s 202` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "202"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused, bound to inform, intentionally omits to give information of an offence (s 202 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `intentionally omits to give information of an offence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed`
    AND f's `intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence`
    AND f's `which he is legally bound to give`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 202 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional omission to give information of an offence by a person bound to inform)
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 202` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `intentionally omits to give information of an offence` f

@export Frame a charge under section 202 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional omission to give information of an offence by a person bound to inform), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 202` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "202" "intentional omission to give information of an offence by a person bound to inform"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 202`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 202` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing or having reason to believe that an offence, namely ", f's `the offence`, ", had been committed, did intentionally omit to give information respecting that offence which you were legally bound to give", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed`) "knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence`) "intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `which he is legally bound to give`) "which he is legally bound to give"),
                (`missing unless` (`intentionally omits to give information of an offence` f) "the elements of section 202 taken together")))

§§ `s 203 - Giving false information respecting an offence committed`

-- 203. Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been
-- committed, gives any information respecting that offence which he knows or believes
-- to be false, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2
-- years, or with fine, or with both.
-- Explanations.-In sections 201 and 202 and in this section "offence" includes any act
-- committed at any place out of Singapore which if committed in Singapore would be
-- punishable under any of the following sections, namely, 302, 304, 382, 392, 393,
-- 394, 395, 396, 397, 399, 402, 435, 436, 449, 450, 459 and 460.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 203
`punishment prescribed by s 203` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "203"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused gives false information respecting an offence (s 203 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `gives false information respecting an offence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed`
    AND f's `gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 203 of the Penal Code 1871 (giving false information respecting an offence committed)
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 203` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `gives false information respecting an offence` f

@export Frame a charge under section 203 of the Penal Code 1871 (giving false information respecting an offence committed), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Offence Information Facts` @desc What the accused knew of an offence, and what the accused did or omitted about it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 203` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "203" "giving false information respecting an offence committed"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 203`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 203` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing or having reason to believe that an offence, namely ", f's `the offence`, ", had been committed, did give information respecting that offence which you knew or believed to be false", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed`) "knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false`) "gives any information respecting that offence which he knows or believes to be false"),
                (`missing unless` (`gives false information respecting an offence` f) "the elements of section 203 taken together")))

§§ `s 204 - Destruction of document or electronic record to prevent its production as evidence`

-- 204. Whoever secretes or destroys any document or electronic record which he may be
-- lawfully compelled to produce as evidence before a court of justice, or in any
-- proceeding lawfully held before a public servant as such, or obliterates or renders
-- illegible the whole or any part of such document or electronic record with the
-- intention of preventing the same from being produced or used as evidence before such
-- court or public servant as aforesaid, or after he has been lawfully summoned or
-- required to produce the same for that purpose, shall be punished with imprisonment
-- for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.

-- FORK JO-5: the intention and "after he has been lawfully summoned" are read as
-- alternatives, each attaching to every act.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 204 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Evidence Document Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `secretes or destroys the document or electronic record`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused secrete or destroy the document or electronic record? (s 204)
    `obliterates or renders illegible the whole or any part of it`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obliterate it, or render the whole or part of it illegible? (s 204)
    `he may be lawfully compelled to produce it as evidence before a court of justice or in a proceeding lawfully held before a public servant as such`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the accused be lawfully compelled to produce it as evidence before a court of justice, or in a proceeding lawfully held before a public servant as such? (s 204)
    `with the intention of preventing it from being produced or used as evidence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to prevent it from being produced or used as evidence before that court or public servant? (s 204) - a fault element
    `after he has been lawfully summoned or required to produce it for that purpose`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the accused been lawfully summoned or required to produce it for that purpose? (s 204)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 204
`punishment prescribed by s 204` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "204"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused secretes, destroys or obliterates a document or electronic record to prevent its production as evidence (s 204 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Evidence Document Facts` @desc The document or electronic record, and what the accused did to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `destroys a document to prevent its production as evidence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (f's `secretes or destroys the document or electronic record` OR f's `obliterates or renders illegible the whole or any part of it`)
    AND f's `he may be lawfully compelled to produce it as evidence before a court of justice or in a proceeding lawfully held before a public servant as such`
    AND (f's `with the intention of preventing it from being produced or used as evidence` OR f's `after he has been lawfully summoned or required to produce it for that purpose`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 204 of the Penal Code 1871 (destruction of document or electronic record to prevent its production as evidence)
GIVEN f IS A `Evidence Document Facts` @desc The document or electronic record, and what the accused did to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 204` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `destroys a document to prevent its production as evidence` f

@export Frame a charge under section 204 of the Penal Code 1871 (destruction of document or electronic record to prevent its production as evidence), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Evidence Document Facts` @desc The document or electronic record, and what the accused did to it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 204` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "204" "destruction of document or electronic record to prevent its production as evidence"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 204`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 204` f)
        (CONCAT "did secrete, destroy, obliterate or render illegible a document or electronic record which you could be lawfully compelled to produce as evidence, with the intention of preventing it from being produced or used as evidence", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `secretes or destroys the document or electronic record` OR f's `obliterates or renders illegible the whole or any part of it`)) "secretes or destroys, or obliterates or renders illegible, any document or electronic record"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `he may be lawfully compelled to produce it as evidence before a court of justice or in a proceeding lawfully held before a public servant as such`) "which he may be lawfully compelled to produce as evidence before a court of justice or a public servant"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `with the intention of preventing it from being produced or used as evidence` OR f's `after he has been lawfully summoned or required to produce it for that purpose`)) "with the intention of preventing its production or use as evidence, or after being lawfully summoned or required to produce it"),
                (`missing unless` (`destroys a document to prevent its production as evidence` f) "the elements of section 204 taken together")))

§§ `s 204A - Obstructing, preventing, perverting or defeating course of justice`

-- 204A. Whoever does an act that has a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or
-- defeat the course of justice -
--    (a) knowing that the act is likely to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the
--      course of justice; or
--    (b) intending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice,
--      shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- Explanation 1.-A mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if
-- he gives false evidence is insufficient to constitute an offence.
-- Explanation 2.-A person sentenced to imprisonment who leaves or attempts to leave
-- Singapore unlawfully to avoid serving that person's sentence has done an act which
-- has a tendency to obstruct and defeat the course of justice.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 204A and its Explanations - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Course of Justice Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `does an act that has a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do an act that has a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice? A person sentenced to imprisonment who leaves or attempts to leave Singapore unlawfully to avoid serving the sentence has done such an act (Explanation 2).
    `knowing that the act is likely to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know that the act was likely to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice? (s 204A(a)) - a fault element
    `intending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice? (s 204A(b)) - a fault element
    `the act is a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if he gives false evidence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act no more than a warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if he gives false evidence? (Explanation 1: that is insufficient)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 204A
`punishment prescribed by s 204A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "204A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused does an act tending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice, with the knowledge or intention s 204A of the Penal Code 1871 requires
GIVEN f IS A `Course of Justice Facts` @desc The act, its tendency, and what the accused knew or intended by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `does an act tending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `does an act that has a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice`
    AND (f's `knowing that the act is likely to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` OR f's `intending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice`)
    AND NOT f's `the act is a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if he gives false evidence`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 204A of the Penal Code 1871 (obstructing, preventing, perverting or defeating the course of justice)
GIVEN f IS A `Course of Justice Facts` @desc The act, its tendency, and what the accused knew or intended by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 204A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `does an act tending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` f

@export Frame a charge under section 204A of the Penal Code 1871 (obstructing, preventing, perverting or defeating the course of justice), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Course of Justice Facts` @desc The act, its tendency, and what the accused knew or intended by it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 204A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "204A" "obstructing, preventing, perverting or defeating the course of justice"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 204A`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 204A` f)
        (CONCAT "did an act which had a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice, ", (IF f's `intending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` THEN "intending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice" ELSE "knowing that the act was likely to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice"), (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `does an act that has a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice`) "does an act that has a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `knowing that the act is likely to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` OR f's `intending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice`)) "(a) knowing that the act is likely to, or (b) intending to, obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice"),
                (`missing unless` (NOT f's `the act is a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if he gives false evidence`) "not a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury (Explanation 1)"),
                (`missing unless` (`does an act tending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` f) "the elements of section 204A taken together")))

§§ `s 204B - Bribery of witnesses`

-- 204B.-(1) Whoever -
--    (a) gives, confers, or procures, promises or offers to give, confer, or procure
--      or attempts to procure, any gratification to, upon, or for any person, upon any
--      agreement or understanding that any person who is aware of any offence (being an
--      offence which any person is legally bound to give information respecting that
--      offence) will abstain from reporting that offence to the police or any agency
--      charged by law with the duty of investigating offences;
--    (b) gives, confers, or procures, promises or offers to give, confer, or procure
--      or attempts to procure, any gratification to, upon, or for any person, upon any
--      agreement or understanding that any person called or to be called as a witness in
--      any judicial proceeding will give false testimony or withhold true testimony or
--      abstain from giving evidence;
--    (c) attempts by any means to induce a person called or to be called as a witness
--      in any judicial proceeding to give false testimony or withhold true testimony or
--      abstain from giving evidence; or
--    (d) asks, receives, or obtains, or agrees or attempts to receive or obtain, any
--      property or benefit of any kind for himself, or any other person, upon any
--      agreement or understanding that any person will as a witness in any judicial
--      proceeding give false testimony or withhold true testimony or abstain from giving
--      evidence, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7
--      years, or with fine, or with both.
-- (2) In this section, "judicial proceeding" means any proceeding in the course of
-- which evidence is or may be legally taken.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 204B - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Witness Bribery Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `gives, confers, procures, promises or offers to give, confer or procure, or attempts to procure, any gratification to, upon or for any person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused give, confer or procure (or promise, offer or attempt to) any gratification to, upon or for any person? (s 204B(1)(a), (b))
    `upon an agreement or understanding that a person aware of an offence which any person is legally bound to report will abstain from reporting it to the police or an investigating agency`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it upon an agreement or understanding that a person aware of an offence (one which someone is legally bound to give information about) would abstain from reporting it to the police or an agency charged by law with investigating offences? (s 204B(1)(a))
    `upon an agreement or understanding that a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding will give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it upon an agreement or understanding that a witness (called or to be called) in a judicial proceeding would give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence? (s 204B(1)(b), (d)) - "judicial proceeding" is any proceeding in which evidence is or may be legally taken (s 204B(2))
    `attempts by any means to induce a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding to give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt by any means to induce such a witness to give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence? (s 204B(1)(c))
    `asks, receives or obtains, or agrees or attempts to receive or obtain, any property or benefit for himself or any other person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused ask for, receive or obtain (or agree or attempt to) any property or benefit for himself or another? (s 204B(1)(d))
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 204B(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 204B` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "204B(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused commits any of the acts in section 204B(1)(a) to (d) of the Penal Code 1871 (bribery of witnesses)
GIVEN f IS A `Witness Bribery Facts` @desc What was given, asked or attempted, and on what understanding about a witness or an offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bribes or suborns a witness` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND ((f's `gives, confers, procures, promises or offers to give, confer or procure, or attempts to procure, any gratification to, upon or for any person` AND f's `upon an agreement or understanding that a person aware of an offence which any person is legally bound to report will abstain from reporting it to the police or an investigating agency`) OR (f's `gives, confers, procures, promises or offers to give, confer or procure, or attempts to procure, any gratification to, upon or for any person` AND f's `upon an agreement or understanding that a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding will give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`) OR f's `attempts by any means to induce a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding to give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence` OR (f's `asks, receives or obtains, or agrees or attempts to receive or obtain, any property or benefit for himself or any other person` AND f's `upon an agreement or understanding that a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding will give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`))

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 204B of the Penal Code 1871 (bribery of witnesses)
GIVEN f IS A `Witness Bribery Facts` @desc What was given, asked or attempted, and on what understanding about a witness or an offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 204B` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `bribes or suborns a witness` f

@export Frame a charge under section 204B of the Penal Code 1871 (bribery of witnesses), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Witness Bribery Facts` @desc What was given, asked or attempted, and on what understanding about a witness or an offence, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 204B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "204B" "bribery of witnesses"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 204B`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 204B` f)
        (CONCAT "did give or offer gratification, or attempt to induce a witness, or ask for or receive a benefit, upon an understanding that an offence would not be reported or that a witness in a judicial proceeding would give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (((f's `gives, confers, procures, promises or offers to give, confer or procure, or attempts to procure, any gratification to, upon or for any person` AND f's `upon an agreement or understanding that a person aware of an offence which any person is legally bound to report will abstain from reporting it to the police or an investigating agency`) OR (f's `gives, confers, procures, promises or offers to give, confer or procure, or attempts to procure, any gratification to, upon or for any person` AND f's `upon an agreement or understanding that a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding will give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`) OR f's `attempts by any means to induce a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding to give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence` OR (f's `asks, receives or obtains, or agrees or attempts to receive or obtain, any property or benefit for himself or any other person` AND f's `upon an agreement or understanding that a person called or to be called as a witness in a judicial proceeding will give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain from giving evidence`))) "(a) gratification for not reporting an offence, (b) gratification for false or withheld testimony, (c) an attempt to induce a witness to give false testimony, withhold true testimony or abstain, or (d) asking or receiving a benefit for that"),
                (`missing unless` (`bribes or suborns a witness` f) "the elements of section 204B taken together")))

§§ `s 205 - False personation for the purpose of any act or proceeding in a suit`

-- 205. Whoever falsely personates another, and in such assumed character makes any
-- admission or statement, or confesses judgment, or causes any process to be issued,
-- or becomes bail or security, or does any other act in any suit or criminal
-- prosecution, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3
-- years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 205 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Personation in Suit Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `falsely personates another`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused falsely personate another person? (s 205)
    `in such assumed character makes an admission or statement, confesses judgment, causes process to be issued, becomes bail or security, or does any other act`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that assumed character, did the accused make an admission or statement, confess judgment, cause process to issue, become bail or security, or do any other act? (s 205)
    `in any suit or criminal prosecution`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in a suit or a criminal prosecution? (s 205)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 205
`punishment prescribed by s 205` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "205"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused falsely personates another for an act or proceeding in a suit or criminal prosecution (s 205 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Personation in Suit Facts` @desc Whom the accused personated, and what the accused did in that character
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falsely personates another in a suit or prosecution` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `falsely personates another`
    AND f's `in such assumed character makes an admission or statement, confesses judgment, causes process to be issued, becomes bail or security, or does any other act`
    AND f's `in any suit or criminal prosecution`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 205 of the Penal Code 1871 (false personation for the purpose of an act or proceeding in a suit)
GIVEN f IS A `Personation in Suit Facts` @desc Whom the accused personated, and what the accused did in that character
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 205` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `falsely personates another in a suit or prosecution` f

@export Frame a charge under section 205 of the Penal Code 1871 (false personation for the purpose of an act or proceeding in a suit), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Personation in Suit Facts` @desc Whom the accused personated, and what the accused did in that character, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 205` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "205" "false personation for the purpose of an act or proceeding in a suit"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 205`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 205` f)
        (CONCAT "did falsely personate another and in such assumed character do an act in a suit or criminal prosecution", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `falsely personates another`) "falsely personates another"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `in such assumed character makes an admission or statement, confesses judgment, causes process to be issued, becomes bail or security, or does any other act`) "in such assumed character makes any admission or statement, confesses judgment, causes process to issue, becomes bail or security, or does any other act"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `in any suit or criminal prosecution`) "in any suit or criminal prosecution"),
                (`missing unless` (`falsely personates another in a suit or prosecution` f) "the elements of section 205 taken together")))

§§ `s 206 - Fraudulent removal or concealment of property to prevent its seizure as a forfeiture, in execution of a decree or under or pursuant to an enforcement order`

-- 206. Whoever fraudulently removes, conceals, transfers, or delivers to any person
-- any property or any interest therein, intending thereby to prevent that property or
-- interest therein from being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine,
-- under a sentence which has been pronounced, or which he knows to be likely to be
-- pronounced by a court of justice or other competent authority, or from being taken
-- in execution of a decree or an order, or under or pursuant to an enforcement order,
-- which has been made, or which he knows to be likely to be made by a court of justice
-- in a civil suit, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 206-210 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Decree Fraud Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `fraudulently`                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25)?
    `removes, conceals, transfers or delivers to any person any property or interest in it`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused remove, conceal, transfer or deliver to anyone any property or interest in property? (s 206)
    `accepts, receives or claims any property or interest in it, knowing that he has no right or rightful claim to it`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused accept, receive or claim property or an interest in it, knowing he had no right or rightful claim to it? (s 207)
    `practises any deception touching any right to any property or interest in it`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused practise any deception touching a right to property or an interest in it? (s 207)
    `intending to prevent it being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence pronounced or known likely to be pronounced`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to prevent the property or interest being taken as a forfeiture, or in satisfaction of a fine, under a sentence pronounced (or known to be likely to be pronounced) by a court or other competent authority? (ss 206, 207)
    `intending to prevent it being taken in execution of a decree or order, or under an enforcement order, made or known likely to be made in a civil suit`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to prevent it being taken in execution of a decree or order, or under or pursuant to an enforcement order, made (or known likely to be made) by a court in a civil suit? (ss 206, 207)
    `causes or suffers a decree or order to be passed against him for a sum not due, a larger sum than is due, or property to which the person is not entitled`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause or suffer a decree or order to be passed against himself at the suit of any person for a sum not due, for more than is due, or for property or an interest to which that person is not entitled? (s 208)
    `causes or suffers a decree or order to be executed or enforced against him after it has been satisfied`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause or suffer a decree or order to be executed or enforced against himself after it had been satisfied, or for anything for which it had been satisfied? (s 208)
    `obtains a decree or order against any person for a sum not due, a larger sum than is due, or property to which he is not entitled`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obtain a decree or order against anyone for a sum not due, for more than is due, or for property or an interest to which the accused is not entitled? (s 210)
    `causes a decree or order to be executed or enforced against any person after it has been satisfied, or suffers or permits any such act in his name`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause a decree or order to be executed or enforced against anyone after it had been satisfied (or for anything for which it had been satisfied), or suffer or permit any such act to be done in his name? (s 210)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 206
`punishment prescribed by s 206` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "206"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused fraudulently removes, conceals, transfers or delivers property to prevent its seizure (s 206 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fraudulently removes or conceals property to prevent its seizure` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's fraudulently
    AND f's `removes, conceals, transfers or delivers to any person any property or interest in it`
    AND (f's `intending to prevent it being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence pronounced or known likely to be pronounced` OR f's `intending to prevent it being taken in execution of a decree or order, or under an enforcement order, made or known likely to be made in a civil suit`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 206 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulent removal or concealment of property to prevent its seizure)
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 206` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `fraudulently removes or conceals property to prevent its seizure` f

@export Frame a charge under section 206 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulent removal or concealment of property to prevent its seizure), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 206` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "206" "fraudulent removal or concealment of property to prevent its seizure"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 206`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 206` f)
        (CONCAT "did fraudulently remove, conceal, transfer or deliver property, intending thereby to prevent it from being taken as a forfeiture, in satisfaction of a fine, or in execution of a decree, order or enforcement order", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `removes, conceals, transfers or delivers to any person any property or interest in it`) "removes, conceals, transfers, or delivers to any person any property or any interest therein"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intending to prevent it being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence pronounced or known likely to be pronounced` OR f's `intending to prevent it being taken in execution of a decree or order, or under an enforcement order, made or known likely to be made in a civil suit`)) "intending thereby to prevent that property or interest from being taken as a forfeiture, in satisfaction of a fine, or in execution of a decree, order or enforcement order"),
                (`missing unless` (`fraudulently removes or conceals property to prevent its seizure` f) "the elements of section 206 taken together")))

§§ `s 207 - Fraudulent claim to property to prevent its seizure as a forfeiture, in execution of a decree or under or pursuant to an enforcement order`

-- 207. Whoever fraudulently accepts, receives or claims any property or any interest
-- therein, knowing that he has no right or rightful claim to such property or
-- interest, or practises any deception touching any right to any property or any
-- interest therein, intending thereby to prevent that property or interest therein
-- from being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence which
-- has been pronounced, or which he knows to be likely to be pronounced by a court of
-- justice or other competent authority, or from being taken in execution of a decree
-- or an order, or under or pursuant to an enforcement order, which has been made or
-- which he knows to be likely to be made by a court of justice in a civil suit, shall
-- be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine,
-- or with both.
-- [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 207
`punishment prescribed by s 207` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "207"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused fraudulently claims property, or practises deception touching a right to it, to prevent its seizure (s 207 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fraudulently claims property to prevent its seizure` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND ((f's fraudulently AND f's `accepts, receives or claims any property or interest in it, knowing that he has no right or rightful claim to it`) OR f's `practises any deception touching any right to any property or interest in it`)
    AND (f's `intending to prevent it being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence pronounced or known likely to be pronounced` OR f's `intending to prevent it being taken in execution of a decree or order, or under an enforcement order, made or known likely to be made in a civil suit`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 207 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulent claim to property to prevent its seizure)
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 207` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `fraudulently claims property to prevent its seizure` f

@export Frame a charge under section 207 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulent claim to property to prevent its seizure), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 207` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "207" "fraudulent claim to property to prevent its seizure"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 207`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 207` f)
        (CONCAT "did fraudulently accept, receive or claim property to which you knew you had no right, or practise deception touching a right to property, intending thereby to prevent it from being taken as a forfeiture, in satisfaction of a fine, or in execution of a decree, order or enforcement order", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (((f's fraudulently AND f's `accepts, receives or claims any property or interest in it, knowing that he has no right or rightful claim to it`) OR f's `practises any deception touching any right to any property or interest in it`)) "fraudulently accepts, receives or claims property knowing he has no right to it, or practises any deception touching any right to property"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intending to prevent it being taken as a forfeiture or in satisfaction of a fine under a sentence pronounced or known likely to be pronounced` OR f's `intending to prevent it being taken in execution of a decree or order, or under an enforcement order, made or known likely to be made in a civil suit`)) "intending thereby to prevent that property or interest from being taken as a forfeiture, in satisfaction of a fine, or in execution of a decree, order or enforcement order"),
                (`missing unless` (`fraudulently claims property to prevent its seizure` f) "the elements of section 207 taken together")))

§§ `s 208 - Fraudulently suffering a decree for a sum not due`

-- 208. Whoever fraudulently causes or suffers a decree or an order to be passed
-- against him at the suit of any person for a sum not due, or for a larger sum than is
-- due to such person, or for any property or interest in property to which such person
-- is not entitled, or fraudulently causes or suffers a decree or an order to be
-- executed or enforced against him after it has been satisfied, or for anything in
-- respect of which it has been satisfied, shall be punished with imprisonment for a
-- term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- Illustration A institutes a suit against Z. Z, knowing that A is likely to obtain a
-- decree against him, fraudulently suffers a judgment to pass against him for a larger
-- amount at the suit of B, who has no just claim against him, in order that B, either
-- on his own account or for the benefit of Z, may share in the proceeds of any sale of
-- Z's property which may be made under A's decree. Z has committed an offence under
-- this section.
-- [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 208
`punishment prescribed by s 208` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "208"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused fraudulently causes or suffers a decree for a sum not due, or its execution after satisfaction (s 208 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fraudulently suffers a decree for a sum not due` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's fraudulently
    AND (f's `causes or suffers a decree or order to be passed against him for a sum not due, a larger sum than is due, or property to which the person is not entitled` OR f's `causes or suffers a decree or order to be executed or enforced against him after it has been satisfied`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 208 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulently suffering a decree for a sum not due)
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 208` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `fraudulently suffers a decree for a sum not due` f

@export Frame a charge under section 208 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulently suffering a decree for a sum not due), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 208` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "208" "fraudulently suffering a decree for a sum not due"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 208`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 208` f)
        (CONCAT "did fraudulently cause or suffer a decree or order to be passed against you for a sum not due, or to be executed or enforced against you after it had been satisfied", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `causes or suffers a decree or order to be passed against him for a sum not due, a larger sum than is due, or property to which the person is not entitled` OR f's `causes or suffers a decree or order to be executed or enforced against him after it has been satisfied`)) "causes or suffers a decree or order to be passed against him for a sum not due or a larger sum, or to be executed after it has been satisfied"),
                (`missing unless` (`fraudulently suffers a decree for a sum not due` f) "the elements of section 208 taken together")))

-- s 209. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]

§§ `s 210 - Fraudulently obtaining a decree for a sum not due`

-- 210. Whoever fraudulently obtains a decree or an order against any person for a sum
-- not due, or for a larger sum than is due, or for any property or interest in
-- property to which he is not entitled, or fraudulently causes a decree or an order to
-- be executed or enforced against any person after it has been satisfied, or for
-- anything in respect of which it has been satisfied, or fraudulently suffers or
-- permits any such act to be done in his name, shall be punished with imprisonment for
-- a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 210
`punishment prescribed by s 210` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "210"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused fraudulently obtains a decree for a sum not due, or causes it to be executed after satisfaction (s 210 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fraudulently obtains a decree for a sum not due` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's fraudulently
    AND (f's `obtains a decree or order against any person for a sum not due, a larger sum than is due, or property to which he is not entitled` OR f's `causes a decree or order to be executed or enforced against any person after it has been satisfied, or suffers or permits any such act in his name`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 210 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulently obtaining a decree for a sum not due)
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 210` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `fraudulently obtains a decree for a sum not due` f

@export Frame a charge under section 210 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulently obtaining a decree for a sum not due), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Decree Fraud Facts` @desc What the accused did with property, a claim or a decree, and what the accused intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 210` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "210" "fraudulently obtaining a decree for a sum not due"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 210`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 210` f)
        (CONCAT "did fraudulently obtain a decree or order against a person for a sum not due, or cause a decree or order to be executed or enforced against a person after it had been satisfied", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `obtains a decree or order against any person for a sum not due, a larger sum than is due, or property to which he is not entitled` OR f's `causes a decree or order to be executed or enforced against any person after it has been satisfied, or suffers or permits any such act in his name`)) "obtains a decree or order for a sum not due or a larger sum, or causes it to be executed after it has been satisfied"),
                (`missing unless` (`fraudulently obtains a decree for a sum not due` f) "the elements of section 210 taken together")))

§§ `s 211 - False charge of offence made with intent to injure`

-- 211. Whoever, with intent to cause injury to any person, institutes or causes to be
-- instituted any criminal proceeding against that person, or falsely charges any
-- person with having committed an offence, knowing that there is no just or lawful
-- ground for such proceeding or charge against that person, shall be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both; and
-- if such criminal proceeding be instituted on a false charge of an offence punishable
-- with death, or imprisonment for 7 years or upwards, shall be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years and shall also be liable to
-- fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 211 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `False Charge Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `with intent to cause injury to any person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to cause injury (s 44) to the person? (s 211) - a fault element
    `institutes or causes to be instituted any criminal proceeding against that person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused institute, or cause to be instituted, a criminal proceeding against the person? (s 211)
    `falsely charges any person with having committed an offence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused falsely charge the person with having committed an offence? (s 211)
    `knowing that there is no just or lawful ground for such proceeding or charge`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know there was no just or lawful ground for the proceeding or charge? (s 211) - a fault element
    `the criminal proceeding is instituted on a false charge of an offence punishable with death, or imprisonment for 7 years or upwards`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a criminal proceeding instituted on a false charge of an offence punishable with death, or with imprisonment for 7 years or upwards (s 41)? (s 211, second limb)
    `the person`                             IS A STRING @desc The person falsely charged, as the charge is to name them
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 211
`punishment prescribed by s 211` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "211"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 211
`punishment prescribed by s 211 (grave offence)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "211"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused, with intent to injure, institutes a criminal proceeding or falsely charges an offence knowing there is no just ground (s 211 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `False Charge Facts` @desc The proceeding or charge, and what the accused knew and intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falsely charges an offence with intent to injure` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `with intent to cause injury to any person`
    AND (f's `institutes or causes to be instituted any criminal proceeding against that person` OR f's `falsely charges any person with having committed an offence`)
    AND f's `knowing that there is no just or lawful ground for such proceeding or charge`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 211 of the Penal Code 1871 (false charge of offence made with intent to injure)
GIVEN f IS A `False Charge Facts` @desc The proceeding or charge, and what the accused knew and intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 211` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `falsely charges an offence with intent to injure` f

@export Frame a charge under section 211 of the Penal Code 1871 (false charge of offence made with intent to injure), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Charge Facts` @desc The proceeding or charge, and what the accused knew and intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 211` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "211" "false charge of offence made with intent to injure"
        (IF f's `the criminal proceeding is instituted on a false charge of an offence punishable with death, or imprisonment for 7 years or upwards` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 211 (grave offence)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 211`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 211` f)
        (CONCAT "did, with intent to cause injury to one ", f's `the person`, ", institute a criminal proceeding against, or falsely charge, that person with having committed an offence, knowing that there was no just or lawful ground for such proceeding or charge", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `with intent to cause injury to any person`) "with intent to cause injury to any person"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `institutes or causes to be instituted any criminal proceeding against that person` OR f's `falsely charges any person with having committed an offence`)) "institutes or causes to be instituted any criminal proceeding against that person, or falsely charges any person with having committed an offence"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that there is no just or lawful ground for such proceeding or charge`) "knowing that there is no just or lawful ground for such proceeding or charge"),
                (`missing unless` (`falsely charges an offence with intent to injure` f) "the elements of section 211 taken together")))

§§ `s 212 - Harbouring an offender`

-- 212.-(1) Whenever an offence has been committed, whoever harbours or conceals a
-- person whom he knows or has reason to believe to be the offender, with the intention
-- of screening him from legal punishment, shall -
--    (a) if the offence is punishable with death, be punished with imprisonment for a
--      term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine;
--    (b) if the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment
--      which may extend to 20 years, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine; and
--    (c) if the offence is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year
--      and not to 20 years, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to one-fourth part of the longest term of imprisonment provided for that
--      offence, or with fine, or with both.
-- (2) In this section, "offence" includes any act committed at any place out of
-- Singapore which if committed in Singapore would be punishable under any of the
-- following sections, namely, 302, 304, 382, 392, 393, 394, 395, 396, 397, 399, 402,
-- 435, 436, 449, 450, 459 and 460, and every such act shall for the purposes of this
-- section be deemed to be punishable as if the accused person had been guilty of it in
-- Singapore.
-- Illustrations
--    (a) A, knowing that B has committed gang-robbery, knowingly conceals B in order
--      to screen him from legal punishment. Here, as B is liable to imprisonment for a
--      term of not less than 5 years and not more than 20 years, A is liable to
--      imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years, and is also liable to fine.
--    (b) A and B are married to each other, and live in their matrimonial home. A
--      knows that B has committed house-breaking. A provides food and shelter to B, with
--      no intention to screen B from legal punishment. A is not guilty of the offence of
--      harbouring.
--    (c) A and B are married to each other, and live in their matrimonial home. A
--      knows that B has committed gang-robbery and is preparing to leave Singapore to
--      evade arrest. A provides food and shelter to B for the purposes of helping B
--      evade detection by the police before he leaves Singapore. A is guilty of the
--      offence of harbouring.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 212, 216, 216A, 216B - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Harbouring Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `harbours the person`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused harbour the person in the ordinary sense? ("harbour" is widened by s 216B)
    `conceals the person`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused conceal the person? (ss 212, 216)
    `supplies the person with shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition, or means of conveyance`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused supply the person with shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition or means of conveyance? (s 216B)
    `assists the person in any way to evade apprehension`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused assist the person in any way to evade apprehension? (s 216B)
    `an offence has been committed`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had an offence been committed? For s 212 it includes an act abroad punishable here under ss 302, 304, 382, 392-397, 399, 402, 435, 436, 449, 450, 459 or 460 (s 212(2)).
    `knows or has reason to believe the person to be the offender`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know, or have reason to believe (s 26), that the person was the offender? (s 212) - a fault element
    `with the intention of screening him from legal punishment`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to screen the person from legal punishment? (s 212) - a fault element; providing food and shelter to a spouse without that intention is not harbouring (illustration (b))
    `the person escaped from lawful custody for an offence of which he was convicted or charged`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the person, convicted of or charged with an offence and in lawful custody for it, escaped from that custody? (s 216(1)); "offence" includes an extraditable act abroad (s 216(2))
    `a public servant in the exercise of lawful powers ordered the person to be apprehended for an offence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had a public servant, exercising lawful powers, ordered the person to be apprehended for an offence? (s 216(1))
    `knowing of such escape or order for apprehension`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know of the escape or the order for apprehension? (s 216) - a fault element
    `with the intention of preventing him from being apprehended`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to prevent the person from being apprehended? (s 216) - a fault element
    `knowing or having reason to believe that the persons are about to commit or have recently committed robbery or gang-robbery`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know or have reason to believe that the persons were about to commit, or had recently committed, robbery or gang-robbery (ss 390, 391, pc-property)? It is immaterial whether within or outside Singapore (s 216A Explanation).
    `with the intention of facilitating the robbery or gang-robbery or of screening them from punishment`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to facilitate the robbery or gang-robbery, or to screen them from punishment? (s 216A) - a fault element
    `the offence is punishable with death`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence (the one screened, harboured or concealed) punishable with death? - its punishment is in its own section, possibly in another group's module
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence punishable with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years?
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year and not to 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence one where "punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year and not to 20 years"? - the words differ from section to section and are the Code's own
    `the person harboured`                   IS A STRING @desc The person harboured or concealed, as the charge is to name them
    `the offence`                            IS A STRING @desc The offence, as it is to be named in the charge - for example "gang-robbery"
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

-- s 216B ("harbour") is encoded below, in its own place; the ss 212, 216 and 216A ladders call it as one box.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 212(1)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 212(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "212(1)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

