@export Whether the accused harbours or conceals an offender with the intention of screening him from legal punishment (s 212(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harbours an offender` f IF
        "Whenever"
    AND f's `an offence has been committed`
    AND (`harbours within section 216B` f OR f's `conceals the person`)
    AND f's `knows or has reason to believe the person to be the offender`
    AND f's `with the intention of screening him from legal punishment`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 212 of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring an offender)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 212` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `harbours an offender` f
    AND (f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year and not to 20 years`)

@export Frame a charge under section 212 of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring an offender), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 212` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "212" "harbouring an offender"
        (IF f's `the offence is punishable with death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 212(a)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 212(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 212(c)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 212` f)
        (CONCAT "did harbour or conceal one ", f's `the person harboured`, ", whom you knew or had reason to believe to be the offender in respect of an offence, namely ", f's `the offence`, ", with the intention of screening that person from legal punishment", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `an offence has been committed`) "whenever an offence has been committed"),
                (`missing unless` ((`harbours within section 216B` f OR f's `conceals the person`)) "harbours or conceals a person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knows or has reason to believe the person to be the offender`) "whom he knows or has reason to believe to be the offender"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of screening him from legal punishment`) "with the intention of screening him from legal punishment"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year and not to 20 years`)) "the offence is punishable with death, with imprisonment for life or up to 20 years, or where it is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year and not to 20 years"),
                (`missing unless` (`harbours an offender` f) "the elements of section 212 taken together")))

§§ `s 213 - Taking gifts, etc., to screen an offender from punishment`

-- 213. Whoever accepts, or agrees to accept, or attempts to obtain any gratification
-- for himself or any other person, or any restitution of property to himself or any
-- other person, in consideration of his concealing an offence, or of his screening any
-- person from legal punishment for any offence, or of his not proceeding against any
-- person for the purpose of bringing him to legal punishment, shall -
--    (a) if the offence is punishable with death, be punished with imprisonment for a
--      term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine;
--    (b) if the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment
--      which may extend to 20 years, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine; and
--    (c) if the offence is punishable with imprisonment not extending to 20 years,
--      shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to one-fourth
--      part of the longest term of imprisonment provided for that offence, or with fine,
--      or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 213-215 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Screening Gift Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `accepts, agrees to accept, or attempts to obtain any gratification or restitution of property for himself or any other person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused accept, agree to accept or attempt to obtain gratification, or restitution of property, for himself or another? (s 213)
    `gives or causes, or offers or agrees to give or cause, any gratification, or to restore or cause the restoration of property, to any person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused give (or cause, offer or agree to give) gratification, or restore (or cause restoration of) property, to any person? (s 214)
    `in consideration of concealing an offence, screening any person from legal punishment for it, or not proceeding against any person to bring him to legal punishment`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in consideration of concealing an offence, screening anyone from legal punishment for it, or not proceeding against anyone to bring him to legal punishment? (ss 213, 214)
    `the offence may lawfully be compounded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the offence lawfully be compounded? (Exception to ss 213 and 214: they do not extend to it)
    `takes, or agrees or consents to take, any gratification under pretence or on account of helping any person to recover movable property of which he has been deprived by an offence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused take (or agree or consent to take) gratification, under pretence or on account of helping someone recover movable property of which he had been deprived by an offence under this Code? (s 215)
    `uses all means in his power to cause the offender to be apprehended and convicted`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused use all means in his power to cause the offender to be apprehended and convicted? (s 215: if so, no offence)
    `the offence is punishable with death`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence (the one screened, harboured or concealed) punishable with death? - its punishment is in its own section, possibly in another group's module
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence punishable with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years?
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment not extending to 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence one where "punishable with imprisonment not extending to 20 years"? - the words differ from section to section and are the Code's own
    `the offence`                            IS A STRING @desc The offence, as it is to be named in the charge - for example "murder"
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

