@export Frame a charge under section 214 of the Penal Code 1871 (offering gift or restoration of property in consideration of screening offender), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Screening Gift Facts` @desc What gratification or restitution was taken, given or offered, and in consideration of what, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 214` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "214" "offering gift or restoration of property in consideration of screening offender"
        (IF f's `the offence is punishable with death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 214(a)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 214(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 214(c)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 214` f)
        (CONCAT "did give or offer gratification, or restore property, to a person in consideration of that person concealing an offence, namely ", f's `the offence`, ", or screening a person from legal punishment for it", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `gives or causes, or offers or agrees to give or cause, any gratification, or to restore or cause the restoration of property, to any person`) "gives or causes, or offers or agrees to give or cause, any gratification, or to restore or cause the restoration of any property"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `in consideration of concealing an offence, screening any person from legal punishment for it, or not proceeding against any person to bring him to legal punishment`) "in consideration of concealing an offence, screening any person from legal punishment, or not proceeding against any person"),
                (`missing unless` (NOT f's `the offence may lawfully be compounded`) "not a case in which the offence may lawfully be compounded (Exception)"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment not extending to 20 years`)) "the offence is punishable with death, with imprisonment for life or up to 20 years, or where it is punishable with imprisonment not extending to 20 years"),
                (`missing unless` (`offers a gift to screen an offender` f) "the elements of section 214 taken together")))

§§ `s 215 - Taking gift to help to recover stolen property, etc.`

-- 215. Whoever takes, or agrees or consents to take, any gratification for himself or
-- any other person under pretence or on account of helping any person to recover any
-- movable property of which he has been deprived by any offence punishable under this
-- Code, shall, unless he uses all means in his power to cause the offender to be
-- apprehended and convicted of the offence, be punished with imprisonment for a term
-- which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 215
`punishment prescribed by s 215` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "215"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused takes gratification on account of helping recover property lost by an offence, without using all means to have the offender apprehended (s 215 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Screening Gift Facts` @desc What gratification or restitution was taken, given or offered, and in consideration of what
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `takes a gift to help recover stolen property` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `takes, or agrees or consents to take, any gratification under pretence or on account of helping any person to recover movable property of which he has been deprived by an offence`
    AND NOT f's `uses all means in his power to cause the offender to be apprehended and convicted`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 215 of the Penal Code 1871 (taking gift to help to recover stolen property)
GIVEN f IS A `Screening Gift Facts` @desc What gratification or restitution was taken, given or offered, and in consideration of what
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 215` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `takes a gift to help recover stolen property` f

@export Frame a charge under section 215 of the Penal Code 1871 (taking gift to help to recover stolen property), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Screening Gift Facts` @desc What gratification or restitution was taken, given or offered, and in consideration of what, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 215` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "215" "taking gift to help to recover stolen property"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 215`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 215` f)
        (CONCAT "did take gratification under pretence or on account of helping a person to recover movable property of which that person had been deprived by an offence, without using all means in your power to cause the offender to be apprehended and convicted", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `takes, or agrees or consents to take, any gratification under pretence or on account of helping any person to recover movable property of which he has been deprived by an offence`) "takes any gratification under pretence or on account of helping any person to recover movable property of which he has been deprived by an offence"),
                (`missing unless` (NOT f's `uses all means in his power to cause the offender to be apprehended and convicted`) "unless he uses all means in his power to cause the offender to be apprehended and convicted"),
                (`missing unless` (`takes a gift to help recover stolen property` f) "the elements of section 215 taken together")))

§§ `s 216 - Harbouring an offender who has escaped from custody, or whose apprehension has been ordered`

-- 216.-(1) Whenever any person convicted of, or charged with an offence, being in
-- lawful custody for that offence, escapes from such custody, or whenever a public
-- servant, in the exercise of the lawful powers of such public servant, orders a
-- certain person to be apprehended for an offence, whoever, knowing of such escape or
-- order for apprehension, harbours or conceals that person with the intention of
-- preventing him from being apprehended, shall be punished in the manner following:
--    (a) if the offence for which the person was in custody, or is ordered to be
--      apprehended, is punishable with death, he shall be punished with imprisonment for
--      a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine;
--    (b) if the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life, or imprisonment
--      which may extend to 20 years, he shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine;
--    (c) if the offence is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year
--      and not to 20 years, he shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to one-fourth part of the longest term of the imprisonment provided for
--      the offence, or with fine, or with both.
-- (2) In this section, "offence" includes also any act or omission of which a person
-- is alleged to have been guilty out of Singapore which if he had been guilty of it in
-- Singapore would have been punishable as an offence and for which he is under any law
-- relating to extradition, or otherwise, liable to be apprehended or detained in
-- custody in Singapore, and every such act or omission shall for the purpose of this
-- section be deemed to be punishable as if the accused person had been guilty of it in
-- Singapore.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 216(1)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 216(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "216(1)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 216(1)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 216(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "216(1)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 216(1)(c)
`punishment prescribed by s 216(c)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "216(1)(c)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one-fourth part of the longest term of imprisonment provided for that offence, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused harbours or conceals a person who has escaped from custody or whose apprehension has been ordered, to prevent apprehension (s 216(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harbours an escaped offender` f IF
        "Whenever"
    AND (f's `the person escaped from lawful custody for an offence of which he was convicted or charged` OR f's `a public servant in the exercise of lawful powers ordered the person to be apprehended for an offence`)
    AND f's `knowing of such escape or order for apprehension`
    AND (`harbours within section 216B` f OR f's `conceals the person`)
    AND f's `with the intention of preventing him from being apprehended`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 216 of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring an offender who has escaped from custody, or whose apprehension has been ordered)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 216` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `harbours an escaped offender` f
    AND (f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year and not to 20 years`)

@export Frame a charge under section 216 of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring an offender who has escaped from custody, or whose apprehension has been ordered), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 216` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "216" "harbouring an offender who has escaped from custody, or whose apprehension has been ordered"
        (IF f's `the offence is punishable with death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 216(a)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 216(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 216(c)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 216` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing that one ", f's `the person harboured`, " had escaped from lawful custody, or had been ordered to be apprehended, for an offence, namely ", f's `the offence`, ", did harbour or conceal that person with the intention of preventing that person from being apprehended", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `the person escaped from lawful custody for an offence of which he was convicted or charged` OR f's `a public servant in the exercise of lawful powers ordered the person to be apprehended for an offence`)) "a person in lawful custody for an offence escapes, or a public servant orders a person to be apprehended for an offence"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing of such escape or order for apprehension`) "knowing of such escape or order for apprehension"),
                (`missing unless` ((`harbours within section 216B` f OR f's `conceals the person`)) "harbours or conceals that person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of preventing him from being apprehended`) "with the intention of preventing him from being apprehended"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year and not to 20 years`)) "the offence is punishable with death, with imprisonment for life or up to 20 years, or where it is punishable with imprisonment which may extend to one year and not to 20 years"),
                (`missing unless` (`harbours an escaped offender` f) "the elements of section 216 taken together")))

§§ `s 216A - Harbouring robbers or gang-robbers, etc.`

-- 216A. Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that any persons are about to
-- commit or have recently committed robbery or gang-robbery, harbours them or any of
-- them with the intention of facilitating the commission of such robbery or gang-
-- robbery or of screening them or any of them from punishment, shall be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to
-- fine.
-- Explanation.- For the purpose of this section it is immaterial whether the robbery
-- or gang-robbery is intended to be committed or has been committed within or without
-- Singapore.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 216A
`punishment prescribed by s 216A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "216A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused harbours persons about to commit, or who have recently committed, robbery or gang-robbery (s 216A of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harbours robbers or gang-robbers` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `knowing or having reason to believe that the persons are about to commit or have recently committed robbery or gang-robbery`
    AND `harbours within section 216B` f
    AND f's `with the intention of facilitating the robbery or gang-robbery or of screening them from punishment`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 216A of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring robbers or gang-robbers)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 216A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `harbours robbers or gang-robbers` f

@export Frame a charge under section 216A of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring robbers or gang-robbers), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 216A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "216A" "harbouring robbers or gang-robbers"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 216A`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 216A` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing or having reason to believe that ", f's `the person harboured`, " were about to commit or had recently committed robbery or gang-robbery, did harbour them with the intention of facilitating the commission of such robbery or gang-robbery or of screening them from punishment", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or having reason to believe that the persons are about to commit or have recently committed robbery or gang-robbery`) "knowing or having reason to believe that any persons are about to commit or have recently committed robbery or gang-robbery"),
                (`missing unless` (`harbours within section 216B` f) "harbours them or any of them"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of facilitating the robbery or gang-robbery or of screening them from punishment`) "with the intention of facilitating the commission of such robbery or gang-robbery or of screening them from punishment"),
                (`missing unless` (`harbours robbers or gang-robbers` f) "the elements of section 216A taken together")))

§§ `s 216B - "Harbour"`

-- 216B. In sections 212, 216 and 216A, "harbour" includes the supplying a person with
-- shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition, or means of conveyance, or
-- the assisting a person in any way to evade apprehension.

@export Whether the accused "harbours" a person, as the word is used in sections 212, 216 and 216A of the Penal Code 1871 (s 216B)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Facts` @desc Whom the accused harboured or concealed, what the accused knew, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harbours within section 216B` f IF
        f's `harbours the person`
    OR  (    "includes the supplying a person with"
         AND f's `supplies the person with shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition, or means of conveyance` )
    OR  (    "or the assisting a person in any way to"
         AND f's `assists the person in any way to evade apprehension` )

§§ `s 217 - Public servant disobeying a direction of law with intent to save person from punishment or property from forfeiture`

-- 217. Whoever, being a public servant, knowingly disobeys any direction of the law as
-- to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant, intending
-- thereby to save, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save, any person
-- from legal punishment, or subject him to a lesser punishment than that to which he
-- is liable, or with intent to save, or knowing that he is likely thereby to save, any
-- property from forfeiture or any charge to which it is liable by law, shall be
-- punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or
-- with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 217-220 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Public Servant Justice Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `being a public servant`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused a public servant (s 21)? - the drill-down is `public servant within section 21` in pc-general
    `knowingly disobeys any direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused knowingly disobey a direction of the law as to how he was to conduct himself as a public servant? (s 217)
    `charged as such public servant with the preparation of any record or other writing`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused, as a public servant, charged with preparing a record or other writing? (s 218)
    `frames that record or writing in a manner which he knows to be incorrect`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused frame it in a manner he knew to be incorrect? (s 218)
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause loss or injury to the public or to any person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend, or know it likely, to cause loss or injury to the public or any person? (s 218) - a fault element
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any person from legal punishment or subject him to a lesser punishment`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend, or know it likely, to save any person from legal punishment (or, for s 217, subject him to a lesser punishment than he is liable to)? (ss 217, 218) - a fault element
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any property from forfeiture or any charge to which it is liable by law`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend, or know it likely, to save property from forfeiture or a charge to which it is liable by law? (ss 217, 218) - a fault element
    `corruptly`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act corruptly? (ss 219, 220) - the Code does not define the word
    `with intent to cause injury to any person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to cause injury (s 44) to any person? (ss 219, 220) - a fault element
    `makes or pronounces in any stage of a judicial proceeding any report, order, verdict or decision`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make or pronounce a report, order, verdict or decision in a stage of a judicial proceeding? (s 219)
    `which he knows to be contrary to law`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it to be contrary to law? (s 219) - a fault element
    `being in an office that gives him legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement, or to keep persons in confinement`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused hold an office giving him legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement, or to keep persons in confinement? (s 220(1))
    `commits a person for trial or to confinement, or keeps a person in confinement, in the exercise of that authority`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the exercise of that authority, did the accused commit a person for trial or to confinement, or keep a person in confinement? (s 220(1)(a))
    `knowing that in doing so he is acting contrary to law`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know that in doing so he was acting contrary to law? (s 220(1)(b)) - a fault element
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 217
`punishment prescribed by s 217` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "217"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant knowingly disobeys a direction of law intending or knowing it likely to save a person from punishment or property from forfeiture (s 217 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disobeys a direction of law to save a person from punishment` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `being a public servant`
    AND f's `knowingly disobeys any direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant`
    AND (f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any person from legal punishment or subject him to a lesser punishment` OR f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any property from forfeiture or any charge to which it is liable by law`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 217 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant disobeying a direction of law with intent to save person from punishment or property from forfeiture)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 217` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `disobeys a direction of law to save a person from punishment` f

@export Frame a charge under section 217 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant disobeying a direction of law with intent to save person from punishment or property from forfeiture), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 217` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "217" "public servant disobeying a direction of law with intent to save person from punishment or property from forfeiture"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 217`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 217` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant, did knowingly disobey a direction of the law as to the way in which you were to conduct yourself as such public servant, intending thereby to save, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby save, a person from legal punishment or property from forfeiture", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `being a public servant`) "being a public servant"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowingly disobeys any direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant`) "knowingly disobeys any direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any person from legal punishment or subject him to a lesser punishment` OR f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any property from forfeiture or any charge to which it is liable by law`)) "intending or knowing it likely thereby to save any person from legal punishment, or any property from forfeiture or charge"),
                (`missing unless` (`disobeys a direction of law to save a person from punishment` f) "the elements of section 217 taken together")))

§§ `s 218 - Public servant framing an incorrect record or writing with intent to save person from punishment, or property from forfeiture`

-- 218. Whoever, being a public servant, and being, as such public servant, charged
-- with the preparation of any record or other writing, frames that record or writing
-- in a manner which he knows to be incorrect, with intent to cause, or knowing it to
-- be likely that he will thereby cause, loss or injury to the public or to any person,
-- or with intent thereby to save, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby
-- save, any person from legal punishment, or with intent to save, or knowing that he
-- is likely thereby to save, any property from forfeiture or other charge to which it
-- is liable by law, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- 3 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 218
`punishment prescribed by s 218` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "218"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant frames a record or writing he knows to be incorrect, with the intent or knowledge s 218 of the Penal Code 1871 requires
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `frames an incorrect record to save a person from punishment` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `being a public servant`
    AND f's `charged as such public servant with the preparation of any record or other writing`
    AND f's `frames that record or writing in a manner which he knows to be incorrect`
    AND (f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause loss or injury to the public or to any person` OR f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any person from legal punishment or subject him to a lesser punishment` OR f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any property from forfeiture or any charge to which it is liable by law`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 218 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant framing an incorrect record or writing with intent to save person from punishment, or property from forfeiture)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 218` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `frames an incorrect record to save a person from punishment` f

@export Frame a charge under section 218 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant framing an incorrect record or writing with intent to save person from punishment, or property from forfeiture), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 218` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "218" "public servant framing an incorrect record or writing with intent to save person from punishment, or property from forfeiture"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 218`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 218` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant charged with the preparation of a record or writing, did frame that record or writing in a manner which you knew to be incorrect, with intent to cause, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby cause, loss or injury, or to save a person from legal punishment or property from forfeiture", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `being a public servant`) "being a public servant"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `charged as such public servant with the preparation of any record or other writing`) "being, as such public servant, charged with the preparation of any record or other writing"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `frames that record or writing in a manner which he knows to be incorrect`) "frames that record or writing in a manner which he knows to be incorrect"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause loss or injury to the public or to any person` OR f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any person from legal punishment or subject him to a lesser punishment` OR f's `intending or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby save any property from forfeiture or any charge to which it is liable by law`)) "with intent to cause, or knowing it likely to cause, loss or injury, or to save any person from legal punishment or property from forfeiture"),
                (`missing unless` (`frames an incorrect record to save a person from punishment` f) "the elements of section 218 taken together")))

§§ `s 219 - Public servant in a judicial proceeding making an order, etc., which he knows to be contrary to law`

-- 219. Whoever, being a public servant, corruptly or with intent to cause injury to
-- any person, makes or pronounces in any stage of a judicial proceeding, any report,
-- order, verdict or decision which he knows to be contrary to law, shall be punished
-- with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with
-- both.
-- [Act 23 of 2021 wef 01/03/2022]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 219
`punishment prescribed by s 219` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "219"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant, corruptly or with intent to injure, makes a report, order, verdict or decision in a judicial proceeding which he knows to be contrary to law (s 219 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes an order in a judicial proceeding known to be contrary to law` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `being a public servant`
    AND (f's corruptly OR f's `with intent to cause injury to any person`)
    AND f's `makes or pronounces in any stage of a judicial proceeding any report, order, verdict or decision`
    AND f's `which he knows to be contrary to law`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 219 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant in a judicial proceeding making an order which he knows to be contrary to law)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 219` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `makes an order in a judicial proceeding known to be contrary to law` f

@export Frame a charge under section 219 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant in a judicial proceeding making an order which he knows to be contrary to law), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 219` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "219" "public servant in a judicial proceeding making an order which he knows to be contrary to law"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 219`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 219` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant, did corruptly or with intent to cause injury to a person make or pronounce in a stage of a judicial proceeding a report, order, verdict or decision which you knew to be contrary to law", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `being a public servant`) "being a public servant"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's corruptly OR f's `with intent to cause injury to any person`)) "corruptly or with intent to cause injury to any person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `makes or pronounces in any stage of a judicial proceeding any report, order, verdict or decision`) "makes or pronounces in any stage of a judicial proceeding any report, order, verdict or decision"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `which he knows to be contrary to law`) "which he knows to be contrary to law"),
                (`missing unless` (`makes an order in a judicial proceeding known to be contrary to law` f) "the elements of section 219 taken together")))

§§ `s 220 - Commitment for trial or confinement by person having authority who knows he is acting contrary to law`

-- 220.-(1) Whoever, being in an office that gives him legal authority to commit
-- persons for trial or to confinement, or to keep persons in confinement -
--    (a) corruptly or with intent to cause injury to any person, commits the person or
--      any other person for trial or to confinement, or keeps the person or any other
--      person in confinement, in the exercise of that authority; and
--    (b) knowing that in doing so he is acting contrary to law, shall be guilty of an
--      offence.
-- (2) Any person convicted of an offence under subsection (1) shall be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term that may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 23 of 2021 wef 01/03/2022]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 220(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 220` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "220(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term that may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a person with legal authority to commit or confine commits or keeps a person in confinement corruptly or with intent to injure, knowing it contrary to law (s 220(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits a person for trial or confinement knowing it contrary to law` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `being in an office that gives him legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement, or to keep persons in confinement`
    AND (f's corruptly OR f's `with intent to cause injury to any person`)
    AND f's `commits a person for trial or to confinement, or keeps a person in confinement, in the exercise of that authority`
    AND f's `knowing that in doing so he is acting contrary to law`

-- s 220(1) defines the offence and s 220(2) punishes it; the charge is laid under
-- section 220 (FORK JO-6 on whether to cite "220(1)" or "220(2)").
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 220 of the Penal Code 1871 (commitment for trial or confinement by person having authority who knows he is acting contrary to law)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 220` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `commits a person for trial or confinement knowing it contrary to law` f

@export Frame a charge under section 220 of the Penal Code 1871 (commitment for trial or confinement by person having authority who knows he is acting contrary to law), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Justice Facts` @desc The public servant's office, what he did, and what he knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 220` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "220" "commitment for trial or confinement by person having authority who knows he is acting contrary to law"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 220`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 220` f)
        (CONCAT "being in an office giving you legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement, did corruptly or with intent to cause injury commit or keep a person in confinement in the exercise of that authority, knowing that in doing so you were acting contrary to law", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `being in an office that gives him legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement, or to keep persons in confinement`) "being in an office that gives him legal authority to commit persons for trial or to confinement, or to keep persons in confinement"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's corruptly OR f's `with intent to cause injury to any person`)) "(a) corruptly or with intent to cause injury to any person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `commits a person for trial or to confinement, or keeps a person in confinement, in the exercise of that authority`) "(a) commits the person for trial or to confinement, or keeps the person in confinement, in the exercise of that authority"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that in doing so he is acting contrary to law`) "(b) knowing that in doing so he is acting contrary to law"),
                (`missing unless` (`commits a person for trial or confinement knowing it contrary to law` f) "the elements of section 220 taken together")))

§§ `s 221 - Intentional omission to apprehend on the part of a public servant bound by law to apprehend`

-- 221. Whoever, being a public servant, legally bound as such public servant to
-- apprehend or to keep in confinement any person charged with or liable to be
-- apprehended for an offence, intentionally omits to apprehend such person, or
-- intentionally suffers such person to escape, or intentionally aids such person in
-- escaping or attempting to escape from such confinement, shall be punished -
--    (a) with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine, if the person in confinement, or who ought to have been
--      apprehended, was charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence
--      punishable with death;
--    (b) with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine, if the person in confinement, or who ought to have been
--      apprehended, was charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence
--      punishable with imprisonment for life, or imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 20 years; or
--    (c) with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or
--      with both, if the person in confinement, or who ought to have been apprehended,
--      was charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence punishable with
--      imprisonment for a term less than 20 years.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 221-223, 225A - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Escape by Public Servant Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `being a public servant`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused a public servant (s 21)? - the drill-down is `public servant within section 21` in pc-general
    `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused, as a public servant, legally bound to apprehend or keep the person in confinement? (ss 221-223, 225A)
    `the person is charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person charged with, or liable to be apprehended for, an offence? (s 221)
    `the person is under sentence of a court of justice for an offence, or lawfully committed to custody`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person under sentence of a court for an offence, or lawfully committed to custody? (s 222)
    `the person is charged with or convicted of an offence, or lawfully committed to custody`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person charged with or convicted of an offence, or lawfully committed to custody? (s 223)
    `intentionally omits to apprehend the person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally omit to apprehend the person? (ss 221, 222)
    `intentionally suffers the person to escape`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally suffer the person to escape? (ss 221, 222)
    `intentionally aids the person in escaping or attempting to escape from confinement`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally aid the person in escaping or attempting to escape? (ss 221, 222)
    `negligently suffers the person to escape from confinement`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused negligently (s 26F) suffer the person to escape from confinement? (s 223)
    `the case is not provided for in section 221, 222 or 223, or in any other law for the time being in force`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case one NOT provided for in s 221, 222 or 223 or in any other law in force? (s 225A)
    `omits to apprehend the person or suffers him to escape from confinement`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused omit to apprehend the person, or suffer him to escape from confinement? (s 225A)
    `does so intentionally`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do so intentionally? (s 225A(a))
    `does so negligently`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do so negligently? (s 225A(b))
    `the offence is punishable with death`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence the person was charged with or liable to be apprehended for punishable with death? (s 221(a))
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life, or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence punishable with imprisonment for life, or for a term which may extend to 20 years? (s 221(b))
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for a term less than 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence punishable with imprisonment for a term less than 20 years? (s 221(c))
    `the person is under sentence of death`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person under sentence of death? (s 222(a))
    `the person is subject by a sentence of a court of justice, or by commutation, to imprisonment for a term of 20 years or upwards`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person subject, by a court's sentence or its commutation, to imprisonment for 20 years or upwards? (s 222(b))
    `the person is subject by a sentence of a court of justice to imprisonment for a term less than 20 years, or was lawfully committed to custody`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person subject by a court's sentence to imprisonment for less than 20 years, or was he lawfully committed to custody? (s 222(c))
    `the person`                             IS A STRING @desc The person concerned, as the charge is to name them
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 221(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 221(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "221(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 221(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 221(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "221(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 221(c)
`punishment prescribed by s 221(c)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "221(c)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant bound to apprehend or confine a person charged with or liable to apprehension for an offence intentionally omits to apprehend him, or suffers or aids his escape (s 221 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `intentionally omits to apprehend a person charged with an offence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `being a public servant`
    AND f's `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`
    AND f's `the person is charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence`
    AND (f's `intentionally omits to apprehend the person` OR f's `intentionally suffers the person to escape` OR f's `intentionally aids the person in escaping or attempting to escape from confinement`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 221 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional omission to apprehend on the part of a public servant bound by law to apprehend)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 221` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `intentionally omits to apprehend a person charged with an offence` f
    AND (f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life, or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for a term less than 20 years`)

@export Frame a charge under section 221 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional omission to apprehend on the part of a public servant bound by law to apprehend), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 221` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "221" "intentional omission to apprehend on the part of a public servant bound by law to apprehend"
        (IF f's `the offence is punishable with death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 221(a)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life, or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 221(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 221(c)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 221` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant legally bound to apprehend or keep in confinement a person charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence, did intentionally omit to apprehend that person, or intentionally suffer or aid that person to escape", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `being a public servant`) "being a public servant"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`) "legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the person is charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence`) "any person charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intentionally omits to apprehend the person` OR f's `intentionally suffers the person to escape` OR f's `intentionally aids the person in escaping or attempting to escape from confinement`)) "intentionally omits to apprehend such person, or intentionally suffers such person to escape, or intentionally aids such person in escaping or attempting to escape"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `the offence is punishable with death` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life, or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years` OR f's `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for a term less than 20 years`)) "the offence is punishable with death, with imprisonment for life or up to 20 years, or with imprisonment for a term less than 20 years"),
                (`missing unless` (`intentionally omits to apprehend a person charged with an offence` f) "the elements of section 221 taken together")))

§§ `s 222 - Intentional omission to apprehend on the part of a public servant bound by law to apprehend person under sentence of a court of justice`

-- 222. Whoever, being a public servant, legally bound as such public servant to
-- apprehend or to keep in confinement any person under sentence of a court of justice
-- for any offence, or lawfully committed to custody, intentionally omits to apprehend
-- such person, or intentionally suffers such person to escape, or intentionally aids
-- such person in escaping or attempting to escape from such confinement, shall be
-- punished -
--    (a) with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--      to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine, if the person in confinement, or
--      who ought to have been apprehended, is under sentence of death;
--    (b) with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine, if the person in confinement, or who ought to have been
--      apprehended, is subject, by a sentence of a court of justice, or by virtue of a
--      commutation of such sentence, to imprisonment for a term of 20 years or upwards;
--      or
--    (c) with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine or
--      with both, if the person in confinement, or who ought to have been apprehended,
--      is subject, by a sentence of a court of justice, to imprisonment for a term less
--      than 20 years, or if the person was lawfully committed to custody.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 222(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 222(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "222(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 222(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 222(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "222(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 222(c)
`punishment prescribed by s 222(c)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "222(c)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant bound to apprehend or confine a person under sentence or lawfully committed to custody intentionally omits to apprehend him, or suffers or aids his escape (s 222 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `intentionally omits to apprehend a person under sentence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `being a public servant`
    AND f's `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`
    AND f's `the person is under sentence of a court of justice for an offence, or lawfully committed to custody`
    AND (f's `intentionally omits to apprehend the person` OR f's `intentionally suffers the person to escape` OR f's `intentionally aids the person in escaping or attempting to escape from confinement`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 222 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional omission to apprehend on the part of a public servant bound by law to apprehend person under sentence of a court of justice)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 222` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `intentionally omits to apprehend a person under sentence` f
    AND (f's `the person is under sentence of death` OR f's `the person is subject by a sentence of a court of justice, or by commutation, to imprisonment for a term of 20 years or upwards` OR f's `the person is subject by a sentence of a court of justice to imprisonment for a term less than 20 years, or was lawfully committed to custody`)

@export Frame a charge under section 222 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional omission to apprehend on the part of a public servant bound by law to apprehend person under sentence of a court of justice), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 222` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "222" "intentional omission to apprehend on the part of a public servant bound by law to apprehend person under sentence of a court of justice"
        (IF f's `the person is under sentence of death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 222(a)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the person is subject by a sentence of a court of justice, or by commutation, to imprisonment for a term of 20 years or upwards` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 222(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 222(c)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 222` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant legally bound to apprehend or keep in confinement a person under sentence of a court of justice or lawfully committed to custody, did intentionally omit to apprehend that person, or intentionally suffer or aid that person to escape", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `being a public servant`) "being a public servant"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`) "legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the person is under sentence of a court of justice for an offence, or lawfully committed to custody`) "any person under sentence of a court of justice for any offence, or lawfully committed to custody"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intentionally omits to apprehend the person` OR f's `intentionally suffers the person to escape` OR f's `intentionally aids the person in escaping or attempting to escape from confinement`)) "intentionally omits to apprehend such person, or intentionally suffers such person to escape, or intentionally aids such person in escaping or attempting to escape"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `the person is under sentence of death` OR f's `the person is subject by a sentence of a court of justice, or by commutation, to imprisonment for a term of 20 years or upwards` OR f's `the person is subject by a sentence of a court of justice to imprisonment for a term less than 20 years, or was lawfully committed to custody`)) "the person is under sentence of death, or of imprisonment, or was lawfully committed to custody"),
                (`missing unless` (`intentionally omits to apprehend a person under sentence` f) "the elements of section 222 taken together")))

§§ `s 223 - Escape from confinement negligently suffered by a public servant`

-- 223. Whoever, being a public servant, legally bound as such public servant to keep
-- in confinement any person charged with or convicted of any offence, or lawfully
-- committed to custody, negligently suffers such person to escape from confinement,
-- shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with
-- fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 223
`punishment prescribed by s 223` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "223"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant bound to keep a person in confinement negligently suffers him to escape (s 223 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `negligently suffers a person to escape` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `being a public servant`
    AND f's `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`
    AND f's `the person is charged with or convicted of an offence, or lawfully committed to custody`
    AND f's `negligently suffers the person to escape from confinement`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 223 of the Penal Code 1871 (escape from confinement negligently suffered by a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 223` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `negligently suffers a person to escape` f

@export Frame a charge under section 223 of the Penal Code 1871 (escape from confinement negligently suffered by a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 223` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "223" "escape from confinement negligently suffered by a public servant"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 223`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 223` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant legally bound to keep in confinement a person charged with or convicted of an offence, or lawfully committed to custody, did negligently suffer that person to escape from confinement", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `being a public servant`) "being a public servant"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`) "legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the person is charged with or convicted of an offence, or lawfully committed to custody`) "any person charged with or convicted of any offence, or lawfully committed to custody"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `negligently suffers the person to escape from confinement`) "negligently suffers such person to escape from confinement"),
                (`missing unless` (`negligently suffers a person to escape` f) "the elements of section 223 taken together")))

§§ `s 224 - Resistance or obstruction by a person to his lawful apprehension`

-- 224. Whoever intentionally offers any resistance or illegal obstruction to the
-- lawful apprehension of himself for any offence with which he is charged, or of which
-- he has been convicted, or escapes or attempts to escape from any custody in which he
-- is lawfully detained for any such offence, shall be punished with imprisonment for a
-- term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- Explanation.- The punishment in this section is in addition to the punishment for
-- which the person to be apprehended or detained in custody was liable for the offence
-- with which he was charged or of which he was convicted.

-- The Explanation (punishment is in addition to that for the original offence) is a
-- sentencing rule, not an element; it rides here as a comment.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 224, 225, 225B - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Escape Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally offer resistance or illegal obstruction to his own lawful apprehension? (ss 224, 225B)
    `for an offence with which he is charged or of which he has been convicted`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that apprehension or custody for an offence with which he was charged or of which he had been convicted? (s 224)
    `escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused escape, or attempt to escape, from custody in which he was lawfully detained? (ss 224, 225B)
    `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally offer resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person? (ss 225, 225B)
    `rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused rescue, or attempt to rescue, another person from custody in which that person was lawfully detained? (ss 225, 225B)
    `the other person is apprehended or detained for an offence`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the other person being apprehended, or detained, for an offence? (s 225)
    `the other person is charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence punishable with imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 225(b))
    `the other person is charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence punishable with death`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 225(c))
    `the other person is liable under a sentence of a court of justice, or by commutation, to imprisonment for a term of 10 years or upwards`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 225(d))
    `the other person is under sentence of death`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 225(e))
    `the case is not provided for in section 224 or 225, or in any other law for the time being in force`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case one NOT provided for in s 224 or 225 or in any other law in force? (s 225B)
    `the person`                             IS A STRING @desc Whose apprehension or custody it was, as the charge is to name them (for ss 225 and 225B)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 224
`punishment prescribed by s 224` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "224"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused intentionally resists his own lawful apprehension, or escapes or attempts to escape lawful custody, for an offence he is charged with or convicted of (s 224 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `resists or escapes lawful apprehension for his own offence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (f's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself` OR f's `escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained`)
    AND f's `for an offence with which he is charged or of which he has been convicted`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 224 of the Penal Code 1871 (resistance or obstruction by a person to his lawful apprehension)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 224` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `resists or escapes lawful apprehension for his own offence` f

@export Frame a charge under section 224 of the Penal Code 1871 (resistance or obstruction by a person to his lawful apprehension), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 224` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "224" "resistance or obstruction by a person to his lawful apprehension"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 224`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 224` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally offer resistance or illegal obstruction to your lawful apprehension, or escape or attempt to escape from custody in which you were lawfully detained, for an offence with which you were charged or of which you had been convicted", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself` OR f's `escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained`)) "intentionally offers any resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself, or escapes or attempts to escape from lawful custody"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `for an offence with which he is charged or of which he has been convicted`) "for any offence with which he is charged, or of which he has been convicted"),
                (`missing unless` (`resists or escapes lawful apprehension for his own offence` f) "the elements of section 224 taken together")))

§§ `s 225 - Resistance or obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person`

-- 225. Whoever intentionally offers any resistance or illegal obstruction to the
-- lawful apprehension of any other person for an offence, or rescues or attempts to
-- rescue any other person from any custody in which that person is lawfully detained
-- for an offence -
--    (a) shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years,
--      or with fine, or with both;
--    (b) if the person to be apprehended, or the person rescued, or attempted to be
--      rescued, is charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence punishable
--      with imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20
--      years, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7
--      years, and shall also be liable to fine;
--    (c) if the person to be apprehended or rescued, or attempted to be rescued, is
--      charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence punishable with death,
--      shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and
--      shall also be liable to fine;
--    (d) if the person to be apprehended or rescued, or attempted to be rescued, is
--      liable, under the sentence of a court of justice, or by virtue of a commutation
--      of such a sentence, to imprisonment for a term of 10 years or upwards, shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall
--      also be liable to fine; or
--    (e) if the person to be apprehended or rescued, or attempted to be rescued, is
--      under sentence of death, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or
--      imprisonment for a term not exceeding 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine.

-- Paragraph (a) is the base punishment; (b)-(e) aggravate it by the other person's
-- situation. Where more than one aggravating paragraph is made out, the charge picks
-- the heaviest in the order (e), (c), (d), (b) - FORK JO-7.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 225(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 225(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225(c)
`punishment prescribed by s 225(c)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225(c)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225(d)
`punishment prescribed by s 225(d)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225(d)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225(e)
`punishment prescribed by s 225(e)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225(e)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused intentionally resists the lawful apprehension of another person for an offence, or rescues or attempts to rescue him from lawful custody (s 225 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `resists the lawful apprehension of another person` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (f's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person` OR f's `rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained`)
    AND f's `the other person is apprehended or detained for an offence`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 225 of the Penal Code 1871 (resistance or obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 225` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `resists the lawful apprehension of another person` f

@export Frame a charge under section 225 of the Penal Code 1871 (resistance or obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 225` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "225" "resistance or obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person"
        (IF f's `the other person is under sentence of death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 225(e)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the other person is charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence punishable with death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 225(c)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the other person is liable under a sentence of a court of justice, or by commutation, to imprisonment for a term of 10 years or upwards` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 225(d)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the other person is charged with or liable to be apprehended for an offence punishable with imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 225(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 225(a)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 225` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally offer resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of one ", f's `the person`, ", or rescue or attempt to rescue that person from lawful custody, for an offence", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person` OR f's `rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained`)) "intentionally offers any resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of any other person, or rescues or attempts to rescue any other person from lawful custody"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the other person is apprehended or detained for an offence`) "for an offence"),
                (`missing unless` (`resists the lawful apprehension of another person` f) "the elements of section 225 taken together")))

§§ `s 225A - Public servant omitting to apprehend or suffering other persons to escape in cases not already provided for`

-- 225A. Whoever, being a public servant, legally bound as such public servant to
-- apprehend or to keep in confinement any person in any case not provided for in
-- section 221, 222 or 223, or in any other law for the time being in force, omits to
-- apprehend that person, or suffers him to escape from confinement, shall be punished
-- -
--    (a) if he does so intentionally, with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--      3 years, or with fine, or with both; or
--    (b) if he does so negligently, with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2
--      years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225A(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 225A(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225A(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225A(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 225A(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225A(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant bound to apprehend or confine a person, in a case not provided for elsewhere, omits to apprehend him or suffers his escape, intentionally or negligently (s 225A of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `omits to apprehend in a case not otherwise provided for` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `being a public servant`
    AND f's `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`
    AND f's `the case is not provided for in section 221, 222 or 223, or in any other law for the time being in force`
    AND f's `omits to apprehend the person or suffers him to escape from confinement`
    AND (f's `does so intentionally` OR f's `does so negligently`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 225A of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant omitting to apprehend or suffering other persons to escape in cases not already provided for)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 225A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `omits to apprehend in a case not otherwise provided for` f

@export Frame a charge under section 225A of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant omitting to apprehend or suffering other persons to escape in cases not already provided for), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Escape by Public Servant Facts` @desc The public servant's duty to apprehend or confine, the person concerned, and what the public servant did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 225A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "225A" "public servant omitting to apprehend or suffering other persons to escape in cases not already provided for"
        (IF f's `does so intentionally` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 225A(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 225A(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 225A` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant legally bound to apprehend or keep in confinement a person, did omit to apprehend that person or suffer that person to escape from confinement", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `being a public servant`) "being a public servant"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person`) "legally bound as such public servant to apprehend or to keep in confinement the person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the case is not provided for in section 221, 222 or 223, or in any other law for the time being in force`) "in any case not provided for in section 221, 222 or 223, or in any other law"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `omits to apprehend the person or suffers him to escape from confinement`) "omits to apprehend that person, or suffers him to escape from confinement"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `does so intentionally` OR f's `does so negligently`)) "(a) intentionally or (b) negligently"),
                (`missing unless` (`omits to apprehend in a case not otherwise provided for` f) "the elements of section 225A taken together")))

§§ `s 225B - Resistance or obstruction to lawful apprehension, or escape, or rescue, in cases not otherwise provided for`

-- 225B. Whoever, in any case not provided for in section 224 or 225, or in any other
-- law for the time being in force, intentionally offers any resistance or illegal
-- obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself or of any other person, or escapes
-- or attempts to escape from any custody in which he is lawfully detained, or rescues
-- or attempts to rescue any other person from any custody in which that person is
-- lawfully detained, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
-- to one year, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225B
`punishment prescribed by s 225B` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225B"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused, in a case not provided for elsewhere, intentionally resists lawful apprehension, escapes lawful custody or rescues another from it (s 225B of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `resists apprehension or escapes in a case not otherwise provided for` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `the case is not provided for in section 224 or 225, or in any other law for the time being in force`
    AND (f's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself` OR f's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person` OR f's `escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained` OR f's `rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 225B of the Penal Code 1871 (resistance or obstruction to lawful apprehension, or escape, or rescue, in cases not otherwise provided for)
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 225B` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `resists apprehension or escapes in a case not otherwise provided for` f

@export Frame a charge under section 225B of the Penal Code 1871 (resistance or obstruction to lawful apprehension, or escape, or rescue, in cases not otherwise provided for), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Escape Facts` @desc The apprehension or custody concerned, and what the accused did to resist it or escape from it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 225B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "225B" "resistance or obstruction to lawful apprehension, or escape, or rescue, in cases not otherwise provided for"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 225B`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 225B` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally offer resistance or illegal obstruction to lawful apprehension, or escape or attempt to escape from lawful custody, or rescue or attempt to rescue another person from lawful custody", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `the case is not provided for in section 224 or 225, or in any other law for the time being in force`) "in any case not provided for in section 224 or 225, or in any other law"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself` OR f's `intentionally offers resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of another person` OR f's `escapes or attempts to escape from custody in which he is lawfully detained` OR f's `rescues or attempts to rescue another person from custody in which that person is lawfully detained`)) "intentionally offers any resistance or illegal obstruction to lawful apprehension, or escapes or attempts to escape from lawful custody, or rescues or attempts to rescue any other person from lawful custody"),
                (`missing unless` (`resists apprehension or escapes in a case not otherwise provided for` f) "the elements of section 225B taken together")))

§§ `s 225C - Offences against laws of Singapore where no special punishment is provided`

-- 225C. Whoever does anything which by any law in force in Singapore he is prohibited
-- from doing, or omits to do anything which he is so enjoined to do, shall, when no
-- special punishment is provided by the law for such commission or omission, be
-- punished with fine not exceeding $2,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225C - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Disobedience of Law Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `does anything which by any law in force in Singapore he is prohibited from doing`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do something a law in force in Singapore prohibits him from doing? (s 225C)
    `omits to do anything which by any law in force in Singapore he is enjoined to do`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused omit to do something a law in force in Singapore enjoins him to do? (s 225C)
    `no special punishment is provided by the law for such commission or omission`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there NO special punishment provided by that law for the act or omission? (s 225C)
    `the law`                                IS A STRING @desc The law prohibiting or enjoining it, as the charge is to name it
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 225C
`punishment prescribed by s 225C` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "225C"
    words                    IS "fine not exceeding $2,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused does what a law in force prohibits, or omits what it enjoins, where no special punishment is provided (s 225C of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Disobedience of Law Facts` @desc What the law in force prohibited or enjoined, and what the accused did or omitted
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disobeys a law where no special punishment is provided` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (f's `does anything which by any law in force in Singapore he is prohibited from doing` OR f's `omits to do anything which by any law in force in Singapore he is enjoined to do`)
    AND f's `no special punishment is provided by the law for such commission or omission`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 225C of the Penal Code 1871 (offences against laws of Singapore where no special punishment is provided)
GIVEN f IS A `Disobedience of Law Facts` @desc What the law in force prohibited or enjoined, and what the accused did or omitted
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 225C` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `disobeys a law where no special punishment is provided` f

@export Frame a charge under section 225C of the Penal Code 1871 (offences against laws of Singapore where no special punishment is provided), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Disobedience of Law Facts` @desc What the law in force prohibited or enjoined, and what the accused did or omitted, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 225C` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "225C" "offences against laws of Singapore where no special punishment is provided"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 225C`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 225C` f)
        (CONCAT "did an act which you were prohibited from doing, or omitted to do an act which you were enjoined to do, by ", f's `the law`, ", for which no special punishment is provided by that law", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `does anything which by any law in force in Singapore he is prohibited from doing` OR f's `omits to do anything which by any law in force in Singapore he is enjoined to do`)) "does anything which by any law in force in Singapore he is prohibited from doing, or omits to do anything which he is so enjoined to do"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `no special punishment is provided by the law for such commission or omission`) "when no special punishment is provided by the law for such commission or omission"),
                (`missing unless` (`disobeys a law where no special punishment is provided` f) "the elements of section 225C taken together")))

-- s 226. [Repealed by Act 31 of 2023 wef 30/05/2025]

-- s 227. [Repealed by Act 1 of 2014]

§§ `s 228 - Intentional insult or interruption to a public servant sitting in any stage of a judicial proceeding or mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process`

-- 228. Whoever intentionally offers any insult or causes any interruption to any
-- public servant, while such public servant is sitting in any stage of a judicial
-- proceeding or conducting any mediation or other alternative dispute resolution
-- process under any written law, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
-- may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both.
-- [Act 18 of 2023 wef 31/01/2024] Personation of an assessor

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 228, 229 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Court Proceedings Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `intentionally offers any insult to a public servant`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally offer an insult to a public servant? (s 228) - for s 228 a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 is not a public servant (s 21(2))
    `intentionally causes any interruption to a public servant`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally cause an interruption to a public servant? (s 228)
    `while the public servant is sitting in any stage of a judicial proceeding`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant then sitting in a stage of a judicial proceeding? (s 228)
    `while the public servant is conducting mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process under written law`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant then conducting a mediation or other ADR process under written law? (s 228)
    `by personation or otherwise, intentionally causes or knowingly suffers himself to be returned, empanelled or sworn as an assessor`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused, by personation or otherwise, intentionally cause or knowingly suffer himself to be returned, empanelled or sworn as an assessor? (s 229)
    `in a case in which he knows that he is not entitled by law to be so returned, empanelled or sworn`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did he know he was not entitled by law to be so returned, empanelled or sworn? (s 229)
    `knowing himself to have been so returned, empanelled or sworn contrary to law, voluntarily serves as such assessor`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Knowing he had been returned, empanelled or sworn contrary to law, did he voluntarily serve as assessor? (s 229)
    `the public servant`                     IS A STRING @desc The public servant, as the charge is to name them
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 228
`punishment prescribed by s 228` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "228"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused intentionally insults or interrupts a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding or conducting ADR under written law (s 228 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Court Proceedings Facts` @desc What the accused did to or in a judicial proceeding or ADR process
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `insults or interrupts a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (f's `intentionally offers any insult to a public servant` OR f's `intentionally causes any interruption to a public servant`)
    AND (f's `while the public servant is sitting in any stage of a judicial proceeding` OR f's `while the public servant is conducting mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process under written law`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 228 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional insult or interruption to a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding)
GIVEN f IS A `Court Proceedings Facts` @desc What the accused did to or in a judicial proceeding or ADR process
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 228` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `insults or interrupts a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding` f

@export Frame a charge under section 228 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional insult or interruption to a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Court Proceedings Facts` @desc What the accused did to or in a judicial proceeding or ADR process, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 228` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "228" "intentional insult or interruption to a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 228`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 228` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally offer an insult or cause an interruption to ", f's `the public servant`, ", a public servant, while sitting in a stage of a judicial proceeding or conducting a mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process under written law", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intentionally offers any insult to a public servant` OR f's `intentionally causes any interruption to a public servant`)) "intentionally offers any insult or causes any interruption to any public servant"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `while the public servant is sitting in any stage of a judicial proceeding` OR f's `while the public servant is conducting mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process under written law`)) "while such public servant is sitting in any stage of a judicial proceeding or conducting any mediation or other ADR process under written law"),
                (`missing unless` (`insults or interrupts a public servant sitting in a judicial proceeding` f) "the elements of section 228 taken together")))

§§ `s 229 - Personation of an assessor Chapter 12 - Offences relating to government stamps`

-- 229. Whoever, by personation or otherwise, intentionally causes or knowingly suffers
-- himself to be returned, empanelled, or sworn as an assessor in any case in which he
-- knows that he is not entitled by law to be so returned, empanelled, or sworn, or
-- knowing himself to have been so returned, empanelled, or sworn contrary to law,
-- voluntarily serves as such assessor, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
-- which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 229
`punishment prescribed by s 229` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "229"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused causes himself to be returned, empanelled or sworn as an assessor knowing he is not entitled, or knowingly serves when wrongly returned (s 229 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Court Proceedings Facts` @desc What the accused did to or in a judicial proceeding or ADR process
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `personates an assessor` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND ((f's `by personation or otherwise, intentionally causes or knowingly suffers himself to be returned, empanelled or sworn as an assessor` AND f's `in a case in which he knows that he is not entitled by law to be so returned, empanelled or sworn`) OR f's `knowing himself to have been so returned, empanelled or sworn contrary to law, voluntarily serves as such assessor`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 229 of the Penal Code 1871 (personation of an assessor)
GIVEN f IS A `Court Proceedings Facts` @desc What the accused did to or in a judicial proceeding or ADR process
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 229` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `personates an assessor` f

@export Frame a charge under section 229 of the Penal Code 1871 (personation of an assessor), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Court Proceedings Facts` @desc What the accused did to or in a judicial proceeding or ADR process, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 229` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "229" "personation of an assessor"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 229`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 229` f)
        (CONCAT "did cause or suffer yourself to be returned, empanelled or sworn as an assessor knowing that you were not entitled by law to be, or knowing yourself to have been so returned contrary to law did voluntarily serve as such assessor", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (((f's `by personation or otherwise, intentionally causes or knowingly suffers himself to be returned, empanelled or sworn as an assessor` AND f's `in a case in which he knows that he is not entitled by law to be so returned, empanelled or sworn`) OR f's `knowing himself to have been so returned, empanelled or sworn contrary to law, voluntarily serves as such assessor`)) "intentionally causes or knowingly suffers himself to be returned, empanelled or sworn as an assessor knowing he is not entitled, or knowingly serves as such assessor contrary to law"),
                (`missing unless` (`personates an assessor` f) "the elements of section 229 taken together")))

