§§ `s 255 - Counterfeiting a Government stamp`

-- 255.-(1) Whoever counterfeits, or knowingly performs any part of the process of
-- counterfeiting, any stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue, shall
-- be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall
-- also be liable to fine.
-- Explanation.-A person who counterfeits by causing a genuine stamp of one
-- denomination to appear like a genuine stamp of a different denomination commits this
-- offence.
-- (2) In this section and sections 256 to 262, a reference to a Government stamp or
-- stamp includes a reference to a stamp certificate issued under the Stamp Duties Act
-- 1929.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 255-263 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Government Stamp Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the stamp concerned (or counterfeited) one issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue? It includes a stamp certificate issued under the Stamp Duties Act 1929 (s 255(2), for ss 255-262).
    `counterfeits the stamp`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused counterfeit the stamp (s 28)? Making a genuine stamp of one denomination appear like a genuine stamp of another is counterfeiting (s 255 Explanation).
    `knowingly performs any part of the process of counterfeiting the stamp`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused knowingly perform any part of the process of counterfeiting it? (s 255(1))
    `has in his possession any instrument or material`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have an instrument or material in his possession? (s 256)
    `makes, performs any part of the process of making, buys, sells or disposes of any instrument`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make (or perform part of the process of making), buy, sell or dispose of an instrument? (s 257)
    `for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for counterfeiting the stamp`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the instrument or material for the purpose of counterfeiting such a stamp, or did the accused know or have reason to believe it was intended to be so used? (ss 256, 257)
    `sells or offers for sale the stamp`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused sell or offer the stamp for sale? (s 258)
    `knows or has reason to believe the stamp to be a counterfeit`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know, or have reason to believe, the stamp to be a counterfeit? (s 258) - a fault element
    `has in his possession the stamp`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have the stamp in his possession? (s 259)
    `knows the stamp to be a counterfeit`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know the stamp to be a counterfeit? (ss 259, 260) - a fault element
    `intending to use or dispose of it as a genuine stamp, or in order that it may be used as a genuine stamp`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to use or dispose of it as genuine, or that it may be used as genuine? (s 259)
    `uses the stamp as genuine`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused use the stamp as genuine? (s 260)
    `fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25) or with intent to cause loss to the Government? (ss 261-263)
    `removes or effaces from a substance bearing the stamp any writing or document for which the stamp has been used`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused remove or efface, from a substance bearing the stamp, a writing or document for which it had been used? (s 261)
    `removes from a writing or document a stamp which has been used for it`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused remove from a writing or document a stamp used for it? (s 261)
    `in order that the stamp may be used for a different writing or document`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that done so the stamp could be used for a different writing or document? (s 261)
    `uses the stamp for any purpose`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused use the stamp for any purpose? (s 262)
    `knows the stamp to have been before used`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know the stamp had been used before? (ss 262, 263) - a fault element
    `erases or removes from the stamp any mark put or impressed upon it for the purpose of denoting that it has been used`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused erase or remove from the stamp a mark denoting that it had been used? (s 263)
    `knowingly has in his possession, or sells or disposes of, a stamp from which such a mark has been erased or removed`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused knowingly possess, or sell or dispose of, a stamp from which such a mark had been erased or removed? (s 263)
    `sells or disposes of a stamp which he knows to have been used`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused sell or dispose of a stamp he knew to have been used? (s 263)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 255(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 255` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "255(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused counterfeits, or knowingly performs part of the process of counterfeiting, a Government revenue stamp (s 255(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counterfeits a Government stamp` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (f's `counterfeits the stamp` OR f's `knowingly performs any part of the process of counterfeiting the stamp`)
    AND f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 255 of the Penal Code 1871 (counterfeiting a Government stamp)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 255` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `counterfeits a Government stamp` f

@export Frame a charge under section 255 of the Penal Code 1871 (counterfeiting a Government stamp), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 255` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "255" "counterfeiting a Government stamp"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 255`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 255` f)
        (CONCAT "did counterfeit, or knowingly perform part of the process of counterfeiting, a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `counterfeits the stamp` OR f's `knowingly performs any part of the process of counterfeiting the stamp`)) "counterfeits, or knowingly performs any part of the process of counterfeiting"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`) "any stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue"),
                (`missing unless` (`counterfeits a Government stamp` f) "the elements of section 255 taken together")))

§§ `s 256 - Having possession of an instrument or material for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp`

-- 256. Whoever has in his possession any instrument or material for the purpose of
-- being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used,
-- for the purpose of counterfeiting any stamp issued by the Government for the purpose
-- of revenue, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7
-- years, and shall also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 256
`punishment prescribed by s 256` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "256"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused commits the acts section 256 of the Penal Code 1871 describes (having possession of an instrument or material for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possesses an instrument for counterfeiting a Government stamp` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `has in his possession any instrument or material`
    AND f's `for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for counterfeiting the stamp`
    AND f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 256 of the Penal Code 1871 (having possession of an instrument or material for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 256` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `possesses an instrument for counterfeiting a Government stamp` f

@export Frame a charge under section 256 of the Penal Code 1871 (having possession of an instrument or material for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 256` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "256" "having possession of an instrument or material for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 256`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 256` f)
        (CONCAT "did have in your possession an instrument or material for the purpose of counterfeiting a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `has in his possession any instrument or material`) "has in his possession any instrument or material"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for counterfeiting the stamp`) "for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for counterfeiting"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`) "any stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue"),
                (`missing unless` (`possesses an instrument for counterfeiting a Government stamp` f) "the elements of section 256 taken together")))

§§ `s 257 - Making or selling an instrument for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp`

-- 257. Whoever makes, performs any part of the process of making, buys, sells or
-- disposes of, any instrument for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having
-- reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for the purpose of counterfeiting
-- any stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue, shall be punished
-- with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable
-- to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 257
`punishment prescribed by s 257` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "257"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused commits the acts section 257 of the Penal Code 1871 describes (making or selling an instrument for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes or sells an instrument for counterfeiting a Government stamp` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `makes, performs any part of the process of making, buys, sells or disposes of any instrument`
    AND f's `for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for counterfeiting the stamp`
    AND f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 257 of the Penal Code 1871 (making or selling an instrument for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 257` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `makes or sells an instrument for counterfeiting a Government stamp` f

@export Frame a charge under section 257 of the Penal Code 1871 (making or selling an instrument for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 257` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "257" "making or selling an instrument for the purpose of counterfeiting a Government stamp"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 257`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 257` f)
        (CONCAT "did make, buy, sell or dispose of an instrument for the purpose of counterfeiting a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `makes, performs any part of the process of making, buys, sells or disposes of any instrument`) "makes, performs any part of the process of making, buys, sells or disposes of, any instrument"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for counterfeiting the stamp`) "for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for counterfeiting"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`) "any stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue"),
                (`missing unless` (`makes or sells an instrument for counterfeiting a Government stamp` f) "the elements of section 257 taken together")))

§§ `s 258 - Sale of counterfeit Government stamp`

-- 258. Whoever sells, or offers for sale, any stamp which he knows or has reason to
-- believe to be a counterfeit of any stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of
-- revenue, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years,
-- and shall also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 258
`punishment prescribed by s 258` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "258"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

