                (`missing unless` (`possesses a counterfeit Government stamp` f) "the elements of section 259 taken together")))

§§ `s 260 - Using as genuine a Government stamp known to be counterfeit`

-- 260. Whoever uses as genuine any stamp, knowing it to be a counterfeit of any stamp
-- issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue, shall be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 260
`punishment prescribed by s 260` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "260"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
