§§ `s 261 - Effacing any writing from a substance bearing a Government stamp, or removing from a document a stamp used for it, with intent to cause loss to Government`

-- 261. Whoever, fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government, removes
-- or effaces from any substance bearing any stamp issued by the Government for the
-- purpose of revenue, any writing or document for which such stamp has been used, or
-- removes from any writing or document a stamp which has been used for such writing or
-- document, in order that such stamp may be used for a different writing or document,
-- shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with
-- fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 261
`punishment prescribed by s 261` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "261"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused commits the acts section 261 of the Penal Code 1871 describes (effacing any writing from a substance bearing a Government stamp, or removing from a document a stamp used for it, with intent to cause loss to Government)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `removes writing from a Government stamp to cause loss to the Government` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government`
    AND (f's `removes or effaces from a substance bearing the stamp any writing or document for which the stamp has been used` OR f's `removes from a writing or document a stamp which has been used for it`)
    AND f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`
    AND f's `in order that the stamp may be used for a different writing or document`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 261 of the Penal Code 1871 (effacing any writing from a substance bearing a Government stamp, or removing from a document a stamp used for it, with intent to cause loss to Government)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 261` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `removes writing from a Government stamp to cause loss to the Government` f

@export Frame a charge under section 261 of the Penal Code 1871 (effacing any writing from a substance bearing a Government stamp, or removing from a document a stamp used for it, with intent to cause loss to Government), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 261` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "261" "effacing any writing from a substance bearing a Government stamp, or removing from a document a stamp used for it, with intent to cause loss to Government"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 261`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 261` f)
        (CONCAT "did fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government remove a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue from the writing for which it had been used, or the writing from it, in order that the stamp may be used for a different writing", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government`) "fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `removes or effaces from a substance bearing the stamp any writing or document for which the stamp has been used` OR f's `removes from a writing or document a stamp which has been used for it`)) "removes or effaces from a substance bearing the stamp the writing for which it was used, or removes from a writing a stamp used for it"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`) "any stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `in order that the stamp may be used for a different writing or document`) "in order that such stamp may be used for a different writing or document"),
                (`missing unless` (`removes writing from a Government stamp to cause loss to the Government` f) "the elements of section 261 taken together")))

§§ `s 262 - Using a Government stamp known to have been before used`

-- 262. Whoever, fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government, uses for
-- any purpose a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue, which he
-- knows to have been before used, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
-- may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both. Erasure of mark denoting that
-- stamp has been used

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 262
`punishment prescribed by s 262` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "262"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused commits the acts section 262 of the Penal Code 1871 describes (using a Government stamp known to have been before used)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `uses a Government stamp known to have been before used` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `fraudulently or with intent to cause loss to the Government`
    AND f's `uses the stamp for any purpose`
    AND f's `a stamp issued by the Government for the purpose of revenue`
    AND f's `knows the stamp to have been before used`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 262 of the Penal Code 1871 (using a Government stamp known to have been before used)
GIVEN f IS A `Government Stamp Facts` @desc The stamp or instrument, and what the accused did with it and knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 262` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `uses a Government stamp known to have been before used` f

